('f1e84f8a-0513-5927-b5cd-bf62802a0b94','e52cfae7-b4f4-5393-a9eb-dd73ecf2ea87',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used to show that each of two or more people does something to the other or others',null,null,'یکدیگر، همدیگر (متقابل)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Susan and Robert kissed each other passionately.","translation":"سوزان و رابرت با اشتیاق یکدیگر را بوسیدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001176200.mp3"},{"sentence":"The girls looked at each other.","translation":"دخترها به هم نگاه کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001176203.mp3"},{"sentence":"They enjoy each other’s company.","translation":"آنها از همراهی یکدیگر لذت می برند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001176201.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('84d96dad-2694-5ac5-984c-524c14fc8512','d72d6dec-e459-5522-8690-a6f2e05a1d47',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the quality of doing something well and effectively, without wasting time, money, or energy','[ uncountable ]',null,'کارایی، بازده؛ بهره‌وری','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['improve/increase efficiency The company is taking steps to improve efficiency and reduce costs. Recent efforts by American business to increase efficiency seem to have failed.','promote efficiency (= develop or encourage efficient ways of doing something ) A competitive market helps to promote efficiency.','greater/increased efficiency In a search for greater efficiency, the two departments have merged.','maximum efficiency (= the most that is possible ) The boat''s design helps it to move with maximum efficiency.','fuel efficiency (= using fuel in an efficient way ) Better fuel efficiency can be achieved by driving more slowly.','energy efficiency (= using energy in an efficient way ) Energy efficiency can play a huge role in reducing pollution.','high efficiency (= used about machines ) The diesel engine offers high efficiency and low fuel consumption.','operating/operational efficiency (= the efficiency with which a machine or system works ) The computer can process this information quickly, without any loss of operating efficiency.','efficiency gains (= increases in efficiency ) New technology introduced by the company has brought efficiency gains.','efficiency savings (= money saved by being more efficient ) Efficiency savings in the industry will inevitably lead to job losses.','efficiency measures (= changes introduced to make something more efficient ) The new efficiency measures are designed to improve the health service.','standards of efficiency Their work led to higher standards of efficiency across the industry.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the efficiency of the train service","translation":"کارایی خدمات قطار","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001637504.mp3"},{"sentence":"considerable advancements in energy efficiency","translation":"پیشرفت های قابل توجه در بهره وری انرژی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001182278.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('1321cd90-e965-5c3f-bf3d-d3a9a5917ca8','d72d6dec-e459-5522-8690-a6f2e05a1d47',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'efficiencies','کارایی، بازده؛ بهره‌وری','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['improve/increase efficiency The company is taking steps to improve efficiency and reduce costs. Recent efforts by American business to increase efficiency seem to have failed.','promote efficiency (= develop or encourage efficient ways of doing something ) A competitive market helps to promote efficiency.','greater/increased efficiency In a search for greater efficiency, the two departments have merged.','maximum efficiency (= the most that is possible ) The boat''s design helps it to move with maximum efficiency.','fuel efficiency (= using fuel in an efficient way ) Better fuel efficiency can be achieved by driving more slowly.','energy efficiency (= using energy in an efficient way ) Energy efficiency can play a huge role in reducing pollution.','high efficiency (= used about machines ) The diesel engine offers high efficiency and low fuel consumption.','operating/operational efficiency (= the efficiency with which a machine or system works ) The computer can process this information quickly, without any loss of operating efficiency.','efficiency gains (= increases in efficiency ) New technology introduced by the company has brought efficiency gains.','efficiency savings (= money saved by being more efficient ) Efficiency savings in the industry will inevitably lead to job losses.','efficiency measures (= changes introduced to make something more efficient ) The new efficiency measures are designed to improve the health service.','standards of efficiency Their work led to higher standards of efficiency across the industry.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('1f7ec4d4-f69c-5e0d-bb23-2cd6dcd6b634','851d912b-e36d-5822-9f0e-1e615a539c75',1,null,null,'spoken & written','relating to electricity',null,null,'برقی، مربوط به برق (تجهیزات)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The fire was caused by an electrical fault .","translation":"آتش سوزی ناشی از نقص برق بوده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001629512.mp3"},{"sentence":"an electrical engineer (= a person who designs and makes electrical equipment )","translation":"مهندس برق (= شخصی که تجهیزات الکتریکی را طراحی و می سازد)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001183783.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('7e44ecf6-7d3a-5017-9d56-e1ce3c525c83','851d912b-e36d-5822-9f0e-1e615a539c75',2,null,null,'spoken & written','using electricity',null,null,'با استفاده از برق','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('fab83da8-deba-5578-902e-35c9450e5c95','016c7267-c878-537f-addf-031e1d5de7df',1,null,null,'spoken & written','electronic equipment , such as computers and televisions , uses electricity that has passed through computer chip s, transistor s etc',null,null,'الکترونیکی، برقی (تجهیزات)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"electronic games","translation":"بازی های الکترونیکی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001184179.mp3"},{"sentence":"an electronic organizer (= a small piece of electronic equipment that you can use to record addresses, phone numbers etc )","translation":"یک سازمان دهنده الکترونیکی (= قطعه کوچکی از تجهیزات الکترونیکی که می توانید برای ضبط آدرس، شماره تلفن و غیره استفاده کنید)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001629572.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('25ab6d50-5216-5453-b50e-bb0f5e32610d','016c7267-c878-537f-addf-031e1d5de7df',2,null,null,'spoken & written','using or produced by electronic equipment',null,null,'استفاده یا تولید شده توسط تجهیزات الکترونیکی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"electronic music","translation":"موسیقی الکترونیک","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001184183.mp3"},{"sentence":"electronic banking","translation":"بانکداری الکترونیک","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001629577.mp3"},{"sentence":"electronic publishing (= a system of producing books, magazines etc in a form that can be read on a computer )","translation":"انتشارات الکترونیکی (= سیستمی برای تولید کتاب، مجلات و غیره به شکلی که در رایانه قابل خواندن باشد)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001629579.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('7aa25656-121e-5c97-9988-3b385529638d','7aeb3f89-1027-508c-8db7-2b622a4025c4',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the condition of having a paid job',null,null,'اشتغال، استخدام؛ کار (حقوقی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['paid employment (= a job for which you receive money ) 51% of women return to paid employment within 5 years of having a child.','full-time/part-time employment Mike is in full-time employment, but his wife is not working.','permanent/temporary employment university graduates entering permanent employment for the first time','long-term/regular employment (= working for the same company for a long time ) She finally found regular employment at a hospital in York.','continuous employment (= working all the time, without any periods being unemployed ) You can join the pension scheme after two years of continuous employment with the company.','give/offer somebody employment He was offered employment in the company’s main office.','provide employment (= offer jobs to people ) The new power station will provide employment for around 400 people.','create employment (= make new jobs ) The government is trying to stimulate the economy and create employment.','find/get employment The men hope to find employment in the construction industry.','obtain/secure employment formal (= get employment ) He found it difficult to obtain employment because of his criminal record.','look for employment ( also seek employment formal ) My son had to leave the farm and seek employment elsewhere.','employment opportunities (= jobs that are available for people to apply for ) There are very few employment opportunities in the area.','employment prospects (= someone’s chances of getting a job ) Better qualifications will improve your employment prospects.','employment rights (= the rights that someone has in their job ) Part-time workers don’t have the same employment rights as full-time staff.','employment levels (= the number of people employed in an area ) Employment levels in the region are above the national average.','employment conditions ( also conditions of employment ) (= details about someone’s employment such as how much they are paid, how much holiday they get etc ) All workers have a right to a fair wage and decent conditions of employment.','an employment contract ( also a contract of employment ) (= an official document stating the details about someone’s employment ) There is a clause in your employment contract covering holiday entitlement.','employment terms ( also terms of employment ) (= the details about someone’s employment that are written in their employment contract, including rules that they must follow ) It’s in the terms of their employment that they can’t go on strike.','loss of employment Closure of the factory will lead to a substantial loss of employment.','somebody’s place of employment formal (= the building where they work ) They had a long journey to their place of employment.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She was offered employment in the sales office.","translation":"به او پیشنهاد کار در دفتر فروش داده شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001187996.mp3"},{"sentence":"terms and conditions of employment","translation":"شرایط و ضوابط استخدام","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645889.mp3"},{"sentence":"The employment prospects for science graduates are excellent.","translation":"چشم انداز استخدام برای فارغ التحصیلان علوم عالی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645892.mp3"},{"sentence":"Steve’s still looking for full-time employment .","translation":"استیو همچنان به دنبال شغل تمام وقت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001187995.mp3"},{"sentence":"the needs of women who combine paid employment and care for their families","translation":"نیازهای زنانی که اشتغال با حقوق و مراقبت از خانواده خود را ترکیب می کنند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645896.mp3"},{"sentence":"21.7% of all those in employment were in part-time jobs.","translation":"21.7 درصد از کل افراد شاغل در مشاغل پاره وقت بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645902.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('dc6730e3-b995-51e1-927b-fcad115da2cc','7aeb3f89-1027-508c-8db7-2b622a4025c4',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the act of paying someone to work for you',null,null,'عمل پرداخت پول به کسی تا برای شما کار کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['paid employment (= a job for which you receive money ) 51% of women return to paid employment within 5 years of having a child.','full-time/part-time employment Mike is in full-time employment, but his wife is not working.','permanent/temporary employment university graduates entering permanent employment for the first time','long-term/regular employment (= working for the same company for a long time ) She finally found regular employment at a hospital in York.','continuous employment (= working all the time, without any periods being unemployed ) You can join the pension scheme after two years of continuous employment with the company.','give/offer somebody employment He was offered employment in the company’s main office.','provide employment (= offer jobs to people ) The new power station will provide employment for around 400 people.','create employment (= make new jobs ) The government is trying to stimulate the economy and create employment.','find/get employment The men hope to find employment in the construction industry.','obtain/secure employment formal (= get employment ) He found it difficult to obtain employment because of his criminal record.','look for employment ( also seek employment formal ) My son had to leave the farm and seek employment elsewhere.','employment opportunities (= jobs that are available for people to apply for ) There are very few employment opportunities in the area.','employment prospects (= someone’s chances of getting a job ) Better qualifications will improve your employment prospects.','employment rights (= the rights that someone has in their job ) Part-time workers don’t have the same employment rights as full-time staff.','employment levels (= the number of people employed in an area ) Employment levels in the region are above the national average.','employment conditions ( also conditions of employment ) (= details about someone’s employment such as how much they are paid, how much holiday they get etc ) All workers have a right to a fair wage and decent conditions of employment.','an employment contract ( also a contract of employment ) (= an official document stating the details about someone’s employment ) There is a clause in your employment contract covering holiday entitlement.','employment terms ( also terms of employment ) (= the details about someone’s employment that are written in their employment contract, including rules that they must follow ) It’s in the terms of their employment that they can’t go on strike.','loss of employment Closure of the factory will lead to a substantial loss of employment.','somebody’s place of employment formal (= the building where they work ) They had a long journey to their place of employment.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Mexican law prohibits the employment of children under 14.","translation":"قانون مکزیک به کارگیری کودکان زیر 14 سال را ممنوع می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645905.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('1d49cf19-d962-5e27-8780-1935cc7538ab','7aeb3f89-1027-508c-8db7-2b622a4025c4',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the number of people who have jobs',null,null,'تعداد افرادی که شغل دارند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['paid employment (= a job for which you receive money ) 51% of women return to paid employment within 5 years of having a child.','full-time/part-time employment Mike is in full-time employment, but his wife is not working.','permanent/temporary employment university graduates entering permanent employment for the first time','long-term/regular employment (= working for the same company for a long time ) She finally found regular employment at a hospital in York.','continuous employment (= working all the time, without any periods being unemployed ) You can join the pension scheme after two years of continuous employment with the company.','give/offer somebody employment He was offered employment in the company’s main office.','provide employment (= offer jobs to people ) The new power station will provide employment for around 400 people.','create employment (= make new jobs ) The government is trying to stimulate the economy and create employment.','find/get employment The men hope to find employment in the construction industry.','obtain/secure employment formal (= get employment ) He found it difficult to obtain employment because of his criminal record.','look for employment ( also seek employment formal ) My son had to leave the farm and seek employment elsewhere.','employment opportunities (= jobs that are available for people to apply for ) There are very few employment opportunities in the area.','employment prospects (= someone’s chances of getting a job ) Better qualifications will improve your employment prospects.','employment rights (= the rights that someone has in their job ) Part-time workers don’t have the same employment rights as full-time staff.','employment levels (= the number of people employed in an area ) Employment levels in the region are above the national average.','employment conditions ( also conditions of employment ) (= details about someone’s employment such as how much they are paid, how much holiday they get etc ) All workers have a right to a fair wage and decent conditions of employment.','an employment contract ( also a contract of employment ) (= an official document stating the details about someone’s employment ) There is a clause in your employment contract covering holiday entitlement.','employment terms ( also terms of employment ) (= the details about someone’s employment that are written in their employment contract, including rules that they must follow ) It’s in the terms of their employment that they can’t go on strike.','loss of employment Closure of the factory will lead to a substantial loss of employment.','somebody’s place of employment formal (= the building where they work ) They had a long journey to their place of employment.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Nationwide employment now stands at 95%.","translation":"اشتغال در سراسر کشور اکنون 95 درصد است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645909.mp3"},{"sentence":"Many economists consider full employment an unrealistic goal.","translation":"بسیاری از اقتصاددانان اشتغال کامل را یک هدف غیر واقعی می دانند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645913.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('2b853f17-1638-5328-84ae-bcae48626893','7aeb3f89-1027-508c-8db7-2b622a4025c4',4,null,null,'formal','the use of a particular object , method , skill etc to achieve something',null,null,'استفاده از یک شیء خاص، روش، مهارت و غیره برای رسیدن به چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Was the employment of force justified?","translation":"آیا استفاده از زور موجه بود؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001188020.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('3df83a3a-a1bc-5ffd-ad76-1cefdfd0e66e','4143df8b-b46b-5724-9bc5-1ed44d87ee0d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a company, organization , or business','[ countable ]',null,'بنگاه، شرکت؛ روحیه تلاش، وکالت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a large/large-scale enterprise The company has grown into a large-scale enterprise that employs hundreds of people.','a small/small-scale enterprise The tax will affect owners of small-scale enterprises consisting of up to ten people.','a successful enterprise She is the owner of an extremely successful enterprise.','a commercial/business enterprise If you are setting up your own business enterprise, your bank can help.','an economic enterprise (= one that is intended to make money ) It''s an economic enterprise, not a charity.','a state/state-owned enterprise ( also a public enterprise British English ) (= one owned by the government ) New Zealand Rail is a state-owned enterprise.','an enterprise zone (= an area created by the government to attract businesses ) Many firms relocate to enterprise zones because of tax incentives.','an enterprise economy (= an economic system in which there are many private businesses ) An enterprise economy can generate wealth and reduce unemployment.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"commercial enterprises such as banks and food manufacturers","translation":"شرکت های تجاری مانند بانک ها و تولید کنندگان مواد غذایی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001625645.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('4598dfbf-a017-50e6-ba85-3ae05dc471f3','4143df8b-b46b-5724-9bc5-1ed44d87ee0d',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the activity of starting and running businesses','[ uncountable ]','free enterprise , private enterprise','فعالیت راه اندازی و راه اندازی مشاغل','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a large/large-scale enterprise The company has grown into a large-scale enterprise that employs hundreds of people.','a small/small-scale enterprise The tax will affect owners of small-scale enterprises consisting of up to ten people.','a successful enterprise She is the owner of an extremely successful enterprise.','a commercial/business enterprise If you are setting up your own business enterprise, your bank can help.','an economic enterprise (= one that is intended to make money ) It''s an economic enterprise, not a charity.','a state/state-owned enterprise ( also a public enterprise British English ) (= one owned by the government ) New Zealand Rail is a state-owned enterprise.','an enterprise zone (= an area created by the government to attract businesses ) Many firms relocate to enterprise zones because of tax incentives.','an enterprise economy (= an economic system in which there are many private businesses ) An enterprise economy can generate wealth and reduce unemployment.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the management of state enterprise (= done by the government )","translation":"مدیریت شرکت دولتی (= توسط دولت انجام می شود)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001625658.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('68de0557-7f88-5f49-8159-9832e1200328','4143df8b-b46b-5724-9bc5-1ed44d87ee0d',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a large and complicated project , especially one that is done with a group of other people','[ countable ]',null,'یک پروژه بزرگ و پیچیده، به خصوص پروژه ای که با گروهی از افراد دیگر انجام می شود',array['initiative']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a large/large-scale enterprise The company has grown into a large-scale enterprise that employs hundreds of people.','a small/small-scale enterprise The tax will affect owners of small-scale enterprises consisting of up to ten people.','a successful enterprise She is the owner of an extremely successful enterprise.','a commercial/business enterprise If you are setting up your own business enterprise, your bank can help.','an economic enterprise (= one that is intended to make money ) It''s an economic enterprise, not a charity.','a state/state-owned enterprise ( also a public enterprise British English ) (= one owned by the government ) New Zealand Rail is a state-owned enterprise.','an enterprise zone (= an area created by the government to attract businesses ) Many firms relocate to enterprise zones because of tax incentives.','an enterprise economy (= an economic system in which there are many private businesses ) An enterprise economy can generate wealth and reduce unemployment.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The programme is a joint enterprise with the London Business School.","translation":"این برنامه یک شرکت مشترک با مدرسه تجارت لندن است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001625666.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('b6f6cf62-d42f-55b1-a21f-d0b41bbf100e','4143df8b-b46b-5724-9bc5-1ed44d87ee0d',4,null,null,'spoken & written','the ability to think of new activities or ideas and make them work','[ uncountable ]',null,'توانایی فکر کردن به فعالیت ها یا ایده های جدید و عملی کردن آنها','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a large/large-scale enterprise The company has grown into a large-scale enterprise that employs hundreds of people.','a small/small-scale enterprise The tax will affect owners of small-scale enterprises consisting of up to ten people.','a successful enterprise She is the owner of an extremely successful enterprise.','a commercial/business enterprise If you are setting up your own business enterprise, your bank can help.','an economic enterprise (= one that is intended to make money ) It''s an economic enterprise, not a charity.','a state/state-owned enterprise ( also a public enterprise British English ) (= one owned by the government ) New Zealand Rail is a state-owned enterprise.','an enterprise zone (= an area created by the government to attract businesses ) Many firms relocate to enterprise zones because of tax incentives.','an enterprise economy (= an economic system in which there are many private businesses ) An enterprise economy can generate wealth and reduce unemployment.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We’re looking for young people with enterprise and creativity.","translation":"ما به دنبال افراد جوان با سرمایه گذاری و خلاقیت هستیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001498185.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('224ffc19-18a3-5402-ae5a-9a3f69a587d2','f2dda222-e1a0-591c-9368-5d1432ae5f30',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a strong feeling of interest and enjoyment about something and an eagerness to be involved in it','[ uncountable ]',null,'شوق، اشتیاق؛ مشوق (خوش‌آمد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have enthusiasm He never had much enthusiasm for work.','show enthusiasm The younger children showed little enthusiasm for the game.','lose (your) enthusiasm The diet started well, but I lost enthusiasm after a while.','arouse/generate enthusiasm formal (= make people feel enthusiastic ) The changes to the timetable failed to arouse enthusiasm amongst the staff.','dampen somebody’s enthusiasm (= cause people to be unenthusiastic ) The rain had dampened our enthusiasm.','share somebody’s enthusiasm I’m afraid I don’t share my husband’s enthusiasm for camping.','fire somebody’s enthusiasm (= make someone feel very enthusiastic ) At high school, Mr Jones really fired my enthusiasm for history.','infectious (= spreading from one person to another ) Her enthusiasm was infectious.','great/much/considerable enthusiasm There was considerable enthusiasm for the idea of a party.','enormous/tremendous enthusiasm He always plays with tremendous enthusiasm.','genuine/real enthusiasm She talked about the project with genuine enthusiasm.','boundless/unbounded enthusiasm formal (= very great ) I’d like to thank the design team for their boundless enthusiasm.','little enthusiasm (= not much enthusiasm ) In the nearby villages, there’s little enthusiasm for the airport.','initial enthusiasm (= happening at the beginning, but not lasting ) After a few months, their initial enthusiasm had started to wane.','renewed enthusiasm (= starting again, with increased energy or interest ) After lunch, she went about the task with renewed enthusiasm.','youthful enthusiasm (= enthusiasm that is typical of young people ) The team has just the right mix of youthful enthusiasm and experience.','with/without enthusiasm The proposal has been greeted with enthusiasm by both parties.','(be) full of enthusiasm (= very enthusiastic ) He entered politics full of enthusiasm, but that gradually disappeared.','be brimming/bursting/bubbling with enthusiasm (= be very excited and enthusiastic ) Andrea’s voice was brimming with enthusiasm when she told John her plans.','be fired (up) with enthusiasm (= be very enthusiastic and keen to do something ) She came back from the course fired up with enthusiasm.','a wave/burst/surge of enthusiasm (= a sudden feeling of enthusiasm ) The new year began with a fresh wave of enthusiasm.','a lack of enthusiasm My lack of enthusiasm for his suggestion made him angry.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Gillian and Darren greeted the speakers with great enthusiasm .","translation":"گیلیان و دارن با اشتیاق فراوان از سخنرانان استقبال کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001625726.mp3"},{"sentence":"We went along to the local diving club, full of enthusiasm .","translation":"ما با شور و شوق به کلوپ غواصی محلی رفتیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001625736.mp3"},{"sentence":"They go about their tasks with little enthusiasm .","translation":"آنها با کمی اشتیاق به انجام وظایف خود می پردازند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001971247.mp3"},{"sentence":"Britain’s apparent lack of enthusiasm for such a scheme","translation":"عدم اشتیاق آشکار بریتانیا برای چنین طرحی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001625732.mp3"},{"sentence":"Employers showed little enthusiasm for the new regulations.","translation":"کارفرمایان اشتیاق کمی نسبت به مقررات جدید نشان دادند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001971251.mp3"},{"sentence":"He shares your enthusiasm for jazz.","translation":"او در اشتیاق شما برای جاز شریک است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001498377.mp3"},{"sentence":"I left university fired with enthusiasm for work.","translation":"با اشتیاق برای کار از دانشگاه اخراج شدم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001971255.mp3"},{"sentence":"A delay of two hours did not dampen their enthusiasm .","translation":"تأخیر دو ساعته از شور و شوق آنها کم نکرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001971259.mp3"}]'::jsonb,8),
('0d48ba0d-8f34-59a6-97af-0092b11c5b65','f2dda222-e1a0-591c-9368-5d1432ae5f30',2,null,null,'formal','an activity or subject that someone is very interested in','[ countable ]',null,'فعالیت یا موضوعی که شخصی به آن علاقه زیادی دارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have enthusiasm He never had much enthusiasm for work.','show enthusiasm The younger children showed little enthusiasm for the game.','lose (your) enthusiasm The diet started well, but I lost enthusiasm after a while.','arouse/generate enthusiasm formal (= make people feel enthusiastic ) The changes to the timetable failed to arouse enthusiasm amongst the staff.','dampen somebody’s enthusiasm (= cause people to be unenthusiastic ) The rain had dampened our enthusiasm.','share somebody’s enthusiasm I’m afraid I don’t share my husband’s enthusiasm for camping.','fire somebody’s enthusiasm (= make someone feel very enthusiastic ) At high school, Mr Jones really fired my enthusiasm for history.','infectious (= spreading from one person to another ) Her enthusiasm was infectious.','great/much/considerable enthusiasm There was considerable enthusiasm for the idea of a party.','enormous/tremendous enthusiasm He always plays with tremendous enthusiasm.','genuine/real enthusiasm She talked about the project with genuine enthusiasm.','boundless/unbounded enthusiasm formal (= very great ) I’d like to thank the design team for their boundless enthusiasm.','little enthusiasm (= not much enthusiasm ) In the nearby villages, there’s little enthusiasm for the airport.','initial enthusiasm (= happening at the beginning, but not lasting ) After a few months, their initial enthusiasm had started to wane.','renewed enthusiasm (= starting again, with increased energy or interest ) After lunch, she went about the task with renewed enthusiasm.','youthful enthusiasm (= enthusiasm that is typical of young people ) The team has just the right mix of youthful enthusiasm and experience.','with/without enthusiasm The proposal has been greeted with enthusiasm by both parties.','(be) full of enthusiasm (= very enthusiastic ) He entered politics full of enthusiasm, but that gradually disappeared.','be brimming/bursting/bubbling with enthusiasm (= be very excited and enthusiastic ) Andrea’s voice was brimming with enthusiasm when she told John her plans.','be fired (up) with enthusiasm (= be very enthusiastic and keen to do something ) She came back from the course fired up with enthusiasm.','a wave/burst/surge of enthusiasm (= a sudden feeling of enthusiasm ) The new year began with a fresh wave of enthusiasm.','a lack of enthusiasm My lack of enthusiasm for his suggestion made him angry.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('53a3e8d1-8515-5f8d-85ee-cc4d038c0443','14ccb09d-d0e0-5b03-a88b-19fb53d2c96c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','having the same value , purpose , job etc as a person or thing of a different kind',null,null,'هم‌ارز، معادل؛ برابر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a qualification which is equivalent to a degree","translation":"مدرکی که معادل مدرک تحصیلی است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001501654.mp3"},{"sentence":"I had no dollars, but offered him an equivalent amount of sterling.","translation":"من دلار نداشتم، اما به او مبلغی معادل پوند پیشنهاد دادم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001501655.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('b1487dcd-d47f-5ece-b991-9a4b6b8dfe3c','7f7656e4-0f88-589a-87cf-e67b95c3ecc1',1,null,null,'spoken & written','something that has the same value, purpose, job etc as something else',null,null,'چیزی که همان ارزش، هدف، شغل و غیره را با چیز دیگری دارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a direct/exact equivalent The word has no direct equivalent in English.','the nearest/closest equivalent The corner store was the closest equivalent we had to a supermarket when I was young.','the modern/modern-day equivalent (of something) Horror films are the modern-day equivalent of morality tales.','an English/American/French etc equivalent Savings and loan associations are the American equivalent of Britain’s building societies.','have an equivalent This institution has no equivalent in any other European country.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The word has no equivalent in English.","translation":"این کلمه در انگلیسی معادلی ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001501674.mp3"},{"sentence":"He had drunk the equivalent of 15 whiskies.","translation":"او معادل 15 ویسکی نوشیده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001642279.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('c1d1339d-fceb-5d37-859e-50c206934e58','2d5d7577-b0ed-5209-b358-f746bad66572',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used to emphasize that something is more important or happens more with one particular thing than with others','[ sentence adverb ]',null,'به‌ویژه، مخصوصاً؛ به‌طور خاص',array['particularly']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I never liked long walks, especially in winter.","translation":"من هرگز پیاده روی طولانی را دوست نداشتم، به خصوص در زمستان.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001218899.mp3"},{"sentence":"Art books are expensive to produce, especially if they contain colour illustrations.","translation":"تولید کتاب های هنری گران است، به خصوص اگر حاوی تصاویر رنگی باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001614495.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('08d5df23-94e0-519b-abe7-5c16ea63a600','2d5d7577-b0ed-5209-b358-f746bad66572',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to a particularly high degree or much more than usual','[ +adj/adverb ]',null,'به درجه ای خاص یا بسیار بیشتر از حد معمول',array['particularly']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I was especially fond of chocolate biscuits.","translation":"من به خصوص به بیسکویت های شکلاتی علاقه داشتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001218904.mp3"},{"sentence":"Feedback is especially important in learning skills.","translation":"بازخورد به ویژه در مهارت های یادگیری اهمیت دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001614496.mp3"},{"sentence":"A depreciation of the dollar would make US exports cheaper and especially so in Japan.","translation":"کاهش ارزش دلار، صادرات ایالات متحده را ارزان‌تر می‌کند، مخصوصاً در ژاپن.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001614497.mp3"},{"sentence":"Graphics are especially well handled in the book.","translation":"گرافیک به ویژه در کتاب به خوبی انجام شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001614501.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('7335b9ba-7562-51a1-98c8-99cc6a696fe2','2d5d7577-b0ed-5209-b358-f746bad66572',3,null,null,'spoken & written','for a particular person, purpose etc',null,null,'برای یک شخص خاص، هدف و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She bought a new pair of trainers especially for the trip.","translation":"او مخصوصاً برای سفر یک جفت مربی جدید خرید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001614505.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('af5e002a-f226-5c41-93cd-5ab0bac9cc96','2d5d7577-b0ed-5209-b358-f746bad66572',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'not especially','به‌ویژه، مخصوصاً؛ به‌طور خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('7b575508-3133-52ec-93b4-5d7587b92ffb','413d4415-172d-5598-93ff-07f236eaf567',1,null,null,'spoken & written','after a long time, or after a lot of things have happened',null,null,'در نهایت، بالاخره؛ سرانجام','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He eventually escaped and made his way back to England.","translation":"او سرانجام فرار کرد و راهی انگلستان شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223307.mp3"},{"sentence":"Eventually, she got a job and moved to London.","translation":"در نهایت او شغلی پیدا کرد و به لندن نقل مکان کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223308.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('5bece0d0-ddf5-5fd1-b24c-55010189a68e','e31b2455-b8a9-53e4-88bd-60a6fcd53607',1,null,null,'spoken & written','each thing or all things',null,null,'همه چیز، هر چیز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Everything was covered in a thick layer of dust.","translation":"همه چیز در لایه ضخیمی از غبار پوشیده شده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223739.mp3"},{"sentence":"I decided to tell her everything.","translation":"تصمیم گرفتم همه چیز را به او بگویم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001643162.mp3"},{"sentence":"Apart from the bus arriving late, everything else seemed to be going according to plan.","translation":"به غیر از دیر رسیدن اتوبوس، به نظر می رسید همه چیز طبق برنامه پیش می رود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001643163.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('3a6d6e86-de3e-5e17-b7d0-3f3243ef1356','e31b2455-b8a9-53e4-88bd-60a6fcd53607',2,null,null,'spoken & written','all the things in your life, work etc',null,null,'تمام چیزهای زندگی شما، کار و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Everything’s fine at the moment.","translation":"در حال حاضر همه چیز خوب است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223748.mp3"},{"sentence":"I felt that everything was going wrong.","translation":"احساس می کردم همه چیز بد پیش می رود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001643167.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('680792e2-92d4-5475-b278-280388284218','e31b2455-b8a9-53e4-88bd-60a6fcd53607',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be/mean everything (to somebody)','همه چیز، هر چیز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('10964afd-b303-510e-88a2-4b80de258f76','e31b2455-b8a9-53e4-88bd-60a6fcd53607',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'have everything','همه چیز، هر چیز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('23a9a56a-e64b-5dd2-8267-a173c7a333a7','e31b2455-b8a9-53e4-88bd-60a6fcd53607',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'and everything','همه چیز، هر چیز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('1eaa5fd7-0a82-5396-86c5-8ab368edff6d','e31b2455-b8a9-53e4-88bd-60a6fcd53607',6,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'have everything going for you','همه چیز، هر چیز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('3c006edc-5e33-5c7a-9149-ef4bb1040967','e31b2455-b8a9-53e4-88bd-60a6fcd53607',7,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'everything but the kitchen sink','همه چیز، هر چیز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('5aa93a38-2f73-5ece-8054-0b7c7fce2979','8173eb0b-ac40-58fd-be1f-223c612fd370',1,null,null,'spoken & written','in or to every place',null,null,'همه‌جا، در هر جا','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’ve looked everywhere but I can’t find the map.","translation":"همه جا را گشتم اما نقشه را پیدا نکردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223788.mp3"},{"sentence":"He’s travelled everywhere in Europe.","translation":"او به همه جای اروپا سفر کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223789.mp3"},{"sentence":"The south should remain dry, but everywhere else will have heavy rain.","translation":"جنوب باید خشک بماند، اما در هر جای دیگر باران شدید خواهد بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001643174.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('ecc104d5-606c-5372-b600-9ff1cb32f2b4','8173eb0b-ac40-58fd-be1f-223c612fd370',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be everywhere','همه‌جا، در هر جا','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('f549db67-cb3b-573f-8b1c-ec39ba66de72','72bdc1fc-d3d2-5374-a171-8bf8b2fe40ab',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the feeling of being excited','[ uncountable ]',null,'هیجان، اشتیاق؛ خشم (هیجان منفی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['cause/generate excitement The arrival of a stranger caused some excitement in the village.','hide/conceal your excitement He tried to hide his excitement, but his voice was shaking.','control/contain your excitement She could hardly control her excitement when I told her the news.','be trembling with excitement (= to be shaking slightly because you are so excited ) Her hands were trembling with excitement as she opened the letter.','somebody''s excitement grows (= it increases ) Her excitement grew as the day of the wedding came nearer.','the excitement wears off (= it gradually becomes less ) The initial excitement of my new job was starting to wear off.','the excitement dies down (= people stop feeling excited ) The excitement after last month''s elections is beginning to die down.','great/enormous/tremendous excitement There is great excitement about the Pope''s visit. The news causes tremendous excitement.','growing/mounting excitement The children waited with growing excitement.','sheer excitement (= a very strong feeling of excitement ) Nothing can beat driving a racing car for sheer excitement.','real/genuine excitement A goal two minutes from the end provided the game''s only genuine excitement.','nervous/restless excitement (= a feeling of being worried and unable to relax ) My nervous excitement increased with each passing minute.','intense excitement (= a very strong feeling of excitement ) I can still remember the intense excitement of going to see my first football match.','heady excitement (= strong excitement about what you might achieve ) Back then, there was the heady excitement of discovering feminism and getting involved in politics.','youthful/childlike excitement Her voice was full of youthful excitement.','be full of/filled with excitement They were full of excitement at the thought of meeting a real movie star.','a sense/feeling of excitement He woke up that morning with a feeling of excitement.','a state of excitement It seemed that the whole country was in a state of excitement.','an air of excitement (= a general feeling of excitement among a group of people ) There was a real air of excitement before the game.','a surge/buzz of excitement (= a sudden feeling of excitement ) As soon as he noticed her name on the list, a surge of excitement ran through him. There is a buzz of excitement inside the stadium.','a flurry of excitement (= an occasion when there is suddenly a lot of excitement about something ) The takeover bid has caused a flurry of excitement in the City.','a ripple of excitement (= a feeling of excitement that spreads through a group of people ) A ripple of excitement went through the audience as the lights dimmed.','a flicker of excitement (= a feeling of excitement that lasts a very short time ) He felt a flicker of excitement when he heard someone mention his name.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the excitement of becoming a parent","translation":"هیجان پدر و مادر شدن","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001226927.mp3"},{"sentence":"The children were filled with excitement at the thought of visiting Disneyland.","translation":"بچه ها از فکر بازدید از دیزنی لند پر از هیجان شدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040052.mp3"},{"sentence":"In all the excitement, I left my wallet behind.","translation":"با تمام هیجان، کیف پولم را جا گذاشتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040053.mp3"},{"sentence":"In his excitement he couldn''t remember her name.","translation":"در هیجانش نتوانست نام او را به خاطر بیاورد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040054.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('a9752ff2-d1db-594a-b13a-eee1fd2183bd','72bdc1fc-d3d2-5374-a171-8bf8b2fe40ab',2,null,null,'spoken & written','an exciting event or situation','[ countable ]',null,'یک رویداد یا موقعیت هیجان انگیز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['cause/generate excitement The arrival of a stranger caused some excitement in the village.','hide/conceal your excitement He tried to hide his excitement, but his voice was shaking.','control/contain your excitement She could hardly control her excitement when I told her the news.','be trembling with excitement (= to be shaking slightly because you are so excited ) Her hands were trembling with excitement as she opened the letter.','somebody''s excitement grows (= it increases ) Her excitement grew as the day of the wedding came nearer.','the excitement wears off (= it gradually becomes less ) The initial excitement of my new job was starting to wear off.','the excitement dies down (= people stop feeling excited ) The excitement after last month''s elections is beginning to die down.','great/enormous/tremendous excitement There is great excitement about the Pope''s visit. The news causes tremendous excitement.','growing/mounting excitement The children waited with growing excitement.','sheer excitement (= a very strong feeling of excitement ) Nothing can beat driving a racing car for sheer excitement.','real/genuine excitement A goal two minutes from the end provided the game''s only genuine excitement.','nervous/restless excitement (= a feeling of being worried and unable to relax ) My nervous excitement increased with each passing minute.','intense excitement (= a very strong feeling of excitement ) I can still remember the intense excitement of going to see my first football match.','heady excitement (= strong excitement about what you might achieve ) Back then, there was the heady excitement of discovering feminism and getting involved in politics.','youthful/childlike excitement Her voice was full of youthful excitement.','be full of/filled with excitement They were full of excitement at the thought of meeting a real movie star.','a sense/feeling of excitement He woke up that morning with a feeling of excitement.','a state of excitement It seemed that the whole country was in a state of excitement.','an air of excitement (= a general feeling of excitement among a group of people ) There was a real air of excitement before the game.','a surge/buzz of excitement (= a sudden feeling of excitement ) As soon as he noticed her name on the list, a surge of excitement ran through him. There is a buzz of excitement inside the stadium.','a flurry of excitement (= an occasion when there is suddenly a lot of excitement about something ) The takeover bid has caused a flurry of excitement in the City.','a ripple of excitement (= a feeling of excitement that spreads through a group of people ) A ripple of excitement went through the audience as the lights dimmed.','a flicker of excitement (= a feeling of excitement that lasts a very short time ) He felt a flicker of excitement when he heard someone mention his name.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We were both new to the excitements of life in the big city.","translation":"هر دوی ما با هیجانات زندگی در شهر بزرگ آشنا شده بودیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001735168.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('678a4745-4be5-5f7f-a960-d77f892e8f04','7d5ead51-bbc5-5e49-a72f-bd6c94985c6c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a show of paintings , photographs , or other objects that people can go to see','[ countable ]',null,'نمایشگاه، معرض نمایش','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have an exhibition The college is having an exhibition of the students’ work in April.','hold/mount/stage an exhibition formal (= have an exhibition ) Hayward Gallery is mounting an impressive exhibition of new British artists.','put on an exhibition (= have an exhibition ) Last summer the museum put on some wonderful exhibitions for children.','host an exhibition formal (= provide the place for an exhibition ) Boston’s Museum of Fine Art hosts temporary exhibitions alongside its permanent collection.','go to an exhibition ( also attend/visit an exhibition formal ) We went to an exhibition of Russian art at the National Gallery.','see an exhibition We also saw an exhibition of paintings by Sydney Lough Thompson, a New Zealand artist.','arrange/organize an exhibition The trust arranged an exhibition of his drawings in New York.','promote an exhibition (= tell the public about it ) Our press officer contacted the local radio and TV stations to promote the exhibition.','a big/large exhibition This is the largest exhibition of its kind that we have ever seen in London.','an important exhibition an important exhibition of twentieth century art','a major exhibition (= large and important ) His work is the subject of a major exhibition at the National Gallery.','a small exhibition The library held a small exhibition showcasing the work of local artists.','a permanent exhibition The museum hosts a permanent exhibition of Boston’s history.','a temporary exhibition Temporary exhibitions are usually held in the basement.','a touring/travelling exhibition (= one that moves from place to place ) The touring exhibition is scheduled to be in Dallas from March until June.','a retrospective exhibition (= one that shows work from the past ) a retrospective exhibition celebrating 150 years of photography','an exhibition centre British English , an exhibition center American English (= a large building for holding exhibitions ) The exhibition will be held in the National Exhibition Centre in Birmingham.','an exhibition hall There’s a large exhibition hall on the ground floor.','an exhibition stand (= a stand for showing things at an exhibition ) He took up his position at the exhibition stand.','exhibition space (= space where exhibitions can be held ) The building provides 125,000 square metres of exhibition space in 12 halls.','an exhibition venue (= a place where exhibitions can be held ) We are still looking for suitable exhibition venues.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"an exhibition of black and white photographs","translation":"نمایشگاهی از عکس های سیاه و سفید","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000540.mp3"},{"sentence":"The museum is staging an exhibition of Picasso’s work.","translation":"این موزه نمایشگاهی از آثار پیکاسو برپا می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001611899.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('285f7d71-b534-56f4-9a45-52f809ed996d','7d5ead51-bbc5-5e49-a72f-bd6c94985c6c',2,null,null,'spoken & written','when something such as a painting is shown in a public place','[ uncountable ]',null,'هنگامی که چیزی مانند یک نقاشی در یک مکان عمومی نشان داده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have an exhibition The college is having an exhibition of the students’ work in April.','hold/mount/stage an exhibition formal (= have an exhibition ) Hayward Gallery is mounting an impressive exhibition of new British artists.','put on an exhibition (= have an exhibition ) Last summer the museum put on some wonderful exhibitions for children.','host an exhibition formal (= provide the place for an exhibition ) Boston’s Museum of Fine Art hosts temporary exhibitions alongside its permanent collection.','go to an exhibition ( also attend/visit an exhibition formal ) We went to an exhibition of Russian art at the National Gallery.','see an exhibition We also saw an exhibition of paintings by Sydney Lough Thompson, a New Zealand artist.','arrange/organize an exhibition The trust arranged an exhibition of his drawings in New York.','promote an exhibition (= tell the public about it ) Our press officer contacted the local radio and TV stations to promote the exhibition.','a big/large exhibition This is the largest exhibition of its kind that we have ever seen in London.','an important exhibition an important exhibition of twentieth century art','a major exhibition (= large and important ) His work is the subject of a major exhibition at the National Gallery.','a small exhibition The library held a small exhibition showcasing the work of local artists.','a permanent exhibition The museum hosts a permanent exhibition of Boston’s history.','a temporary exhibition Temporary exhibitions are usually held in the basement.','a touring/travelling exhibition (= one that moves from place to place ) The touring exhibition is scheduled to be in Dallas from March until June.','a retrospective ex