('140e61c6-124e-53cd-b9cb-2d7665c97e9c','947dbe12-d72f-5ca9-8258-9a82a620c529',7,'skin','پوست','spoken & written','a cream in the same colour as your skin that you put on before the rest of your make-up','[ uncountable ]',null,'کرمی همرنگ پوستتان که قبل از بقیه آرایش هایتان می زنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('7c16624c-3f5f-5c1e-88c4-b9ef6324422b','947dbe12-d72f-5ca9-8258-9a82a620c529',8,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'shake/rock the foundations of something','شالوده، پایه (ساختمان)؛ بنیاد (سازمان)؛ پایه (اندیشه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('f2706709-40da-51f9-9b45-ff6defaf0fd0','9f915d82-4c96-5da6-b3c1-4f1585c17d1b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','very often or many times',null,null,'مکرراً، به‌طور مکرر؛ اغلب','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He was frequently drunk.","translation":"او اغلب مست بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001281400.mp3"},{"sentence":"I often see him. OR I see him a lot .","translation":"من اغلب او را می بینم. یا من او را زیاد می بینم.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,2),
('82ae9448-7b22-52ac-a136-7589cf670224','1394baba-dd14-5f0a-9b01-2e08d6fac7e7',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a relationship between friends','[ countable ]',null,'دوستی، رفاقت؛ دوستی (پیوند)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['start a friendship Their friendship started after they met at a conference.','strike up a friendship He and Matthew struck up a friendship.','form a friendship The two girls soon formed a friendship.','a friendship develops Friendship often develops on the basis of shared interests.','renew a friendship (= become friends again ) They renewed their friendship after the war.','destroy/spoil a friendship Their friendship was spoilt after a fierce argument.','a close friendship Ron had formed a close relationship with Andrea.','a firm friendship (= one that is strong and not likely to change ) I established a firm friendship with Terence.','a lasting friendship This began a lasting friendship between the two women.','a long-standing friendship (= one that has existed for a long time ) There is a long-standing friendship between the two countries.','a lifelong friendship The two men formed a lifelong friendship.','bonds/ties of friendship (= things that connect friends ) They were united by deep bonds of friendship.','a gesture of friendship (= an action which shows that someone is a friend ) He invited us to his house as a gesture of friendship.','an offer of friendship He turned down the King''s offer of friendship.','offer/extend the hand of friendship (= officially say that you want a friendly relationship ) America extended the hand of friendship, but it was rejected.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The friendship between father and youth deepened.","translation":"دوستی پدر و جوانی عمیق تر شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001722662.mp3"},{"sentence":"his friendship with Sam","translation":"دوستی او با سام","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001722665.mp3"},{"sentence":"her close friendship with her aunt","translation":"دوستی نزدیکش با عمه اش","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001722666.mp3"},{"sentence":"a lifelong friendship","translation":"یک دوستی مادام العمر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001722670.mp3"},{"sentence":"The two boys formed a deep and lasting friendship .","translation":"این دو پسر یک دوستی عمیق و پایدار برقرار کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001282102.mp3"},{"sentence":"He and Bob struck up a friendship (= began to be friends ) .","translation":"او و باب با هم دوستی کردند (= شروع به دوستی کردند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001722680.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('b8ce58ec-caf7-5f8a-b028-8539da68c963','1394baba-dd14-5f0a-9b01-2e08d6fac7e7',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the feelings and behaviour that exist between friends','[ uncountable ]',null,'احساسات و رفتاری که بین دوستان وجود دارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['start a friendship Their friendship started after they met at a conference.','strike up a friendship He and Matthew struck up a friendship.','form a friendship The two girls soon formed a friendship.','a friendship develops Friendship often develops on the basis of shared interests.','renew a friendship (= become friends again ) They renewed their friendship after the war.','destroy/spoil a friendship Their friendship was spoilt after a fierce argument.','a close friendship Ron had formed a close relationship with Andrea.','a firm friendship (= one that is strong and not likely to change ) I established a firm friendship with Terence.','a lasting friendship This began a lasting friendship between the two women.','a long-standing friendship (= one that has existed for a long time ) There is a long-standing friendship between the two countries.','a lifelong friendship The two men formed a lifelong friendship.','bonds/ties of friendship (= things that connect friends ) They were united by deep bonds of friendship.','a gesture of friendship (= an action which shows that someone is a friend ) He invited us to his house as a gesture of friendship.','an offer of friendship He turned down the King''s offer of friendship.','offer/extend the hand of friendship (= officially say that you want a friendly relationship ) America extended the hand of friendship, but it was rejected.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I could always rely on Gary for friendship and support.","translation":"من همیشه می توانستم برای دوستی و حمایت به گری تکیه کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001282110.mp3"},{"sentence":"The Indians have extended the hand of friendship (= shown that they want to be friends with another country ) .","translation":"هندی ها دست دوستی دراز کرده اند (= نشان داده اند که می خواهند با کشور دیگری دوست شوند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001722685.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('9fc13d9a-a95a-5093-85ee-bbafbb5bfc39','9503eb45-be0b-5923-b465-f43fc66ef899',1,null,null,'spoken & written','feeling afraid',null,null,'ترسیده، وحشت‌زده',array['scared']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Don’t be frightened. We’re not going to hurt you.","translation":"نترس ما به شما صدمه نمی زنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001737211.mp3"},{"sentence":"I was frightened of being left by myself in the house.","translation":"از اینکه خودم در خانه رها شوم می ترسیدم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001282303.mp3"},{"sentence":"Her father had an awful temper and she was always frightened of him.","translation":"پدرش خلق و خوی بدی داشت و او همیشه از او می ترسید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001737212.mp3"},{"sentence":"The boy was frightened to speak.","translation":"پسر از حرف زدن ترسید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001737215.mp3"},{"sentence":"She’s frightened that her ex-husband will find her.","translation":"او می ترسد که شوهر سابقش او را پیدا کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001282309.mp3"},{"sentence":"To tell the truth, I was frightened to death (= very frightened ) .","translation":"راستش من از مرگ ترسیدم (= خیلی ترسیده بودم).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000562676.mp3"},{"sentence":"a frightened horse","translation":"اسبی ترسیده","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001282300.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('fb8c7938-9cef-58a7-ade5-4f4fa9a1bc56','9ec32002-d281-5030-85f4-0d5998033616',1,null,null,'spoken & written','all people of about the same age','[ countable ]',null,'نسل، نسل‌ها؛ تولید (برق)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['my/your/their etc generation I consider myself a typical Japanese woman of my generation.','future generations We need to preserve the planet for future generations.','the younger generation The party needs to make its policies appeal to the younger generation too.','the older generation These beliefs were common among the older generation.','the new generation (= younger people, especially people who use new ways of doing something ) He is one of the new generation of English players.','the next generation People want to pass on money to the next generation when they die.','successive/succeeding generations (= generations that follow one another ) This medical textbook has been used by successive generations of medical students and doctors.','earlier generations As with earlier generations of his family, he had been educated at Bootham School, York.','the previous/preceding generation He was the equal of any of the previous generation of great explorers.','later generations For later generations, however, the chances of getting work on leaving school were much lower.','the baby-boom generation (= people born between 1946 and 1964 ) Healthcare expenses are expected to rise as the baby-boom generation reaches retirement.','the generation gap (= the difference between people of different generations ) This study explores the generation gap between parents and their teenage children.','hand something down from generation to generation Native Australians hand down stories and songs from generation to generation.','pass something from one generation to the next Traditional customs are passed from one generation to the next.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Like most of my generation, I had never known a war.","translation":"مانند بسیاری از هم نسلانم، هرگز جنگی را ندیده بودم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001726088.mp3"},{"sentence":"In my generation the divorce rate is very high.","translation":"در نسل من آمار طلاق بسیار بالاست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001288381.mp3"},{"sentence":"the need to preserve the planet for future generations","translation":"نیاز به حفظ سیاره برای نسل های آینده","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001726089.mp3"},{"sentence":"the post-war generation of writers","translation":"نسل نویسندگان پس از جنگ","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001726095.mp3"},{"sentence":"The younger generation don’t know what hard work is.","translation":"نسل جوان نمی دانند کار سخت چیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001288385.mp3"},{"sentence":"The story has been handed down from generation to generation .","translation":"داستان از نسلی به نسل دیگر منتقل شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001726099.mp3"},{"sentence":"This generation has grown up using Internet technology.","translation":"این نسل با استفاده از فناوری اینترنت رشد کرده است.","audio_url":null},{"sentence":"This generation have grown up using Internet technology.","translation":"این نسل با استفاده از فناوری اینترنت بزرگ شده اند.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,8),
('45ee5676-12b5-5ed8-90d0-a6615e885c99','9ec32002-d281-5030-85f4-0d5998033616',2,null,null,'spoken & written','all the members of a family of about the same age','[ countable ]',null,'همه اعضای یک خانواده تقریباً همسن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['my/your/their etc generation I consider myself a typical Japanese woman of my generation.','future generations We need to preserve the planet for future generations.','the younger generation The party needs to make its policies appeal to the younger generation too.','the older generation These beliefs were common among the older generation.','the new generation (= younger people, especially people who use new ways of doing something ) He is one of the new generation of English players.','the next generation People want to pass on money to the next generation when they die.','successive/succeeding generations (= generations that follow one another ) This medical textbook has been used by successive generations of medical students and doctors.','earlier generations As with earlier generations of his family, he had been educated at Bootham School, York.','the previous/preceding generation He was the equal of any of the previous generation of great explorers.','later generations For later generations, however, the chances of getting work on leaving school were much lower.','the baby-boom generation (= people born between 1946 and 1964 ) Healthcare expenses are expected to rise as the baby-boom generation reaches retirement.','the generation gap (= the difference between people of different generations ) This study explores the generation gap between parents and their teenage children.','hand something down from generation to generation Native Australians hand down stories and songs from generation to generation.','pass something from one generation to the next Traditional customs are passed from one generation to the next.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"In those days it was common for three generations of the same family to live together.","translation":"در آن روزها زندگی مشترک سه نسل از یک خانواده معمول بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00381.mp3"},{"sentence":"first-generation immigrants","translation":"مهاجران نسل اول","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001726109.mp3"},{"sentence":"a third-generation American","translation":"یک آمریکایی نسل سوم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001726110.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('a0be9587-adde-575b-bcad-8fed302d19c9','9ec32002-d281-5030-85f4-0d5998033616',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the average period of time between the birth of a person and the birth of that person’s children','[ countable ]',null,'میانگین فاصله زمانی بین تولد یک فرد و تولد فرزندان آن شخص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Some families have lived here for generations.","translation":"برخی از خانواده ها برای نسل ها در اینجا زندگی می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001726111.mp3"},{"sentence":"The country’s attitude toward government is harsher than it was a generation ago.","translation":"نگرش کشور نسبت به دولت خشن تر از یک نسل قبل است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001288401.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('860e5690-5886-5589-9071-6cf7d45e14ef','9ec32002-d281-5030-85f4-0d5998033616',4,null,null,'spoken & written','a group of things that were developed from something else, or from which better things were developed','[ countable ]',null,'گروهی از چیزهایی که از چیز دیگری ساخته شده اند یا چیزهای بهتری از آنها ایجاد شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the new generation of mobile phones","translation":"نسل جدید تلفن های همراه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001288406.mp3"},{"sentence":"the first generation of nuclear power stations","translation":"نسل اول نیروگاه های هسته ای","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001726118.mp3"},{"sentence":"second-generation computers","translation":"کامپیوترهای نسل دوم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001726121.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('c31bdb2a-f12b-5a96-8b6c-2245a9ed6fa3','9ec32002-d281-5030-85f4-0d5998033616',5,null,null,'spoken & written','the process of producing something or making something happen','[ uncountable ]',null,'فرآیند تولید چیزی یا به وقوع پیوستن چیزی',array['production']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the generation of electricity","translation":"تولید برق","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001288411.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ac3d2666-ce50-52a7-a75d-20fd0ca850f8','25647809-1c5b-5cad-b535-5e0a6b6b8cfe',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a girl or woman that you are having a romantic relationship with',null,null,'دوست‌دختر، دوست‌دختر (نو)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He’s never had a girlfriend .","translation":"او هرگز دوست دختر نداشته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001718459.mp3"},{"sentence":"He lives in Chicago with his girlfriend.","translation":"او با دوست دخترش در شیکاگو زندگی می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001718463.mp3"},{"sentence":"one of my ex-girlfriends (= former girlfriends )","translation":"یکی از دوست دخترهای سابق من (= دوست دختر سابق)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001718467.mp3"},{"sentence":"I didn’t have a steady girlfriend (= one you have a long relationship with ) .","translation":"من دوست دختر ثابتی نداشتم (= دوست دختری که با او رابطه طولانی دارید).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001718471.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('549fec4e-e977-58ba-806c-1c496ea6a3ee','25647809-1c5b-5cad-b535-5e0a6b6b8cfe',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a woman or girl’s female friend',null,null,'دوست زن یک زن یا دختر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She’s out with one of her girlfriends.","translation":"او با یکی از دوست دخترش بیرون است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001296972.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('473e60d5-4d9d-521a-86bf-d21631d186df','d24b6259-a674-5436-b846-60706f3ca0a6',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used to say goodbye when you are leaving someone or they are leaving at night , or before going to sleep',null,null,'شب بخیر (هنگام خداحافظی شبانه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Good night. Sleep well.","translation":"شب بخیر خوب بخواب.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001328467.mp3"},{"sentence":"Night night , darling. See you in the morning.","translation":"شب شب عزیزم صبح میبینمت","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,2),
('f811f02c-7420-5b9b-abec-f827f66785dd','e2c1cc5c-1739-5b9a-9346-e72d655c16f1',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the group of people who govern a country or state','[ countable usually singular ]',null,'دولت، حاکمیت؛ حکومت، مدیریت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the UK/French/Thai etc government The UK government has offered to send aid.','the Labour/Conservative/Social Democratic etc government In August 1931, the Labour government collapsed.','the Thatcher/Blair etc government Did the Blair government do more for Africa than previous ones?','a coalition government (= government made up of members of more than one political party ) The country has had a succession of weak coalition governments.','a minority government (= that does not have enough politicians to control parliament ) His party had gained only enough seats to form a minority government.','a left-wing/right-wing government The new left-wing government restructured the economy.','central/national government (= that deals with national rather than local things ) Funding will continue to be available from central government for further education for adults.','federal government (= in the US, the government of the whole country rather than of the individual states ) The state, rather than the federal government, would have to pay the extra cost.','local/state/city government The interference in local government by central government is not just financial, but political.','government spending Government spending on health care totals about $60 billion a year.','a government minister A government minister said that there would be an inquiry.','a government official (= someone who works for a government in an official position ) He had a meeting with French scientists and government officials.','a government body ( also a government agency American English ) (= an organization run by the government ) Patents are granted by the U.K. Patent Office, a government body.','a government department the government department responsible for policing','elect a government (= vote to choose a government ) A new government was elected last October.','form a government (= become the government ) The party attained the majority of seats it needed to form a government.','bring down a government (= force it to lose power ) It was a major scandal that nearly brought down the government.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The Government are planning further cuts in public spending.","translation":"دولت در حال برنامه ریزی برای کاهش بیشتر هزینه های عمومی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001330193.mp3"},{"sentence":"The US government has tightened restrictions on firearms.","translation":"دولت آمریکا محدودیت‌های مربوط به سلاح گرم را تشدید کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001708674.mp3"},{"sentence":"Neither party had the majority necessary to form a government.","translation":"هیچ یک از احزاب اکثریت لازم برای تشکیل دولت را نداشتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001708675.mp3"},{"sentence":"Structural reforms are unlikely under the present government.","translation":"اصلاحات ساختاری در دولت کنونی بعید است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001330207.mp3"},{"sentence":"The government is planning to increase taxes.","translation":"دولت در حال برنامه ریزی برای افزایش مالیات است.","audio_url":null},{"sentence":"The government are planning to increase taxes.","translation":"دولت در حال برنامه ریزی برای افزایش مالیات است.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,6),
('6dbdf29a-4044-5fbf-a418-34661861a9b7','e2c1cc5c-1739-5b9a-9346-e72d655c16f1',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a form or system of government','[ uncountable ]','local government , central government','یک شکل یا سیستم حکومتی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the UK/French/Thai etc government The UK government has offered to send aid.','the Labour/Conservative/Social Democratic etc government In August 1931, the Labour government collapsed.','the Thatcher/Blair etc government Did the Blair government do more for Africa than previous ones?','a coalition government (= government made up of members of more than one political party ) The country has had a succession of weak coalition governments.','a minority government (= that does not have enough politicians to control parliament ) His party had gained only enough seats to form a minority government.','a left-wing/right-wing government The new left-wing government restructured the economy.','central/national government (= that deals with national rather than local things ) Funding will continue to be available from central government for further education for adults.','federal government (= in the US, the government of the whole country rather than of the individual states ) The state, rather than the federal government, would have to pay the extra cost.','local/state/city government The interference in local government by central government is not just financial, but political.','government spending Government spending on health care totals about $60 billion a year.','a government minister A government minister said that there would be an inquiry.','a government official (= someone who works for a government in an official position ) He had a meeting with French scientists and government officials.','a government body ( also a government agency American English ) (= an organization run by the government ) Patents are granted by the U.K. Patent Office, a government body.','a government department the government department responsible for policing','elect a government (= vote to choose a government ) A new government was elected last October.','form a government (= become the government ) The party attained the majority of seats it needed to form a government.','bring down a government (= force it to lose power ) It was a major scandal that nearly brought down the government.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Most people in the country support the return to democratic government.","translation":"اکثر مردم این کشور از بازگشت به حکومت دموکراتیک حمایت می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001330212.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('feb42bbc-8da4-5d50-b248-adecdc83a9e5','e2c1cc5c-1739-5b9a-9346-e72d655c16f1',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the process or way of governing','[ uncountable ]',null,'فرآیند یا شیوه حکومت داری','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the UK/French/Thai etc government The UK government has offered to send aid.','the Labour/Conservative/Social Democratic etc government In August 1931, the Labour government collapsed.','the Thatcher/Blair etc government Did the Blair government do more for Africa than previous ones?','a coalition government (= government made up of members of more than one political party ) The country has had a succession of weak coalition governments.','a minority government (= that does not have enough politicians to control parliament ) His party had gained only enough seats to form a minority government.','a left-wing/right-wing government The new left-wing government restructured the economy.','central/national government (= that deals with national rather than local things ) Funding will continue to be available from central government for further education for adults.','federal government (= in the US, the government of the whole country rather than of the individual states ) The state, rather than the federal government, would have to pay the extra cost.','local/state/city government The interference in local government by central government is not just financial, but political.','government spending Government spending on health care totals about $60 billion a year.','a government minister A government minister said that there would be an inquiry.','a government official (= someone who works for a government in an official position ) He had a meeting with French scientists and government officials.','a government body ( also a government agency American English ) (= an organization run by the government ) Patents are granted by the U.K. Patent Office, a government body.','a government department the government department responsible for policing','elect a government (= vote to choose a government ) A new government was elected last October.','form a government (= become the government ) The party attained the majority of seats it needed to form a government.','bring down a government (= force it to lose power ) It was a major scandal that nearly brought down the government.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"What would the opposition do if they were in government (= governing the country ) ?","translation":"اگر اپوزیسیون در حکومت بودند (= اداره کشور) چه می کردند؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001708696.mp3"},{"sentence":"the importance of good government in developing countries","translation":"اهمیت دولت خوب در کشورهای در حال توسعه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001708703.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('008ca13a-6c78-55a8-b4aa-4064003885a8','e2c1cc5c-1739-5b9a-9346-e72d655c16f1',4,null,null,'spoken & written','the degree to which the government controls economic and social activities','[ uncountable ]',null,'درجه ای که دولت فعالیت های اقتصادی و اجتماعی را کنترل می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the UK/French/Thai etc government The UK government has offered to send aid.','the Labour/Conservative/Social Democratic etc government In August 1931, the Labour government collapsed.','the Thatcher/Blair etc government Did the Blair government do more for Africa than previous ones?','a coalition government (= government made up of members of more than one political party ) The country has had a succession of weak coalition governments.','a minority government (= that does not have enough politicians to control parliament ) His party had gained only enough seats to form a minority government.','a left-wing/right-wing government The new left-wing government restructured the economy.','central/national government (= that deals with national rather than local things ) Funding will continue to be available from central government for further education for adults.','federal government (= in the US, the government of the whole country rather than of the individual states ) The state, rather than the federal government, would have to pay the extra cost.','local/state/city government The interference in local government by central government is not just financial, but political.','government spending Government spending on health care totals about $60 billion a year.','a government minister A government minister said that there would be an inquiry.','a government official (= someone who works for a government in an official position ) He had a meeting with French scientists and government officials.','a government body ( also a government agency American English ) (= an organization run by the government ) Patents are granted by the U.K. Patent Office, a government body.','a government department the government department responsible for policing','elect a government (= vote to choose a government ) A new government was elected last October.','form a government (= become the government ) The party attained the majority of seats it needed to form a government.','bring down a government (= force it to lose power ) It was a major scandal that nearly brought down the government.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The protest march was really about big government (= when the government controls many activities ) .","translation":"راهپیمایی اعتراضی واقعاً درباره دولت بزرگ بود (= زمانی که دولت بسیاری از فعالیت ها را کنترل می کند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001330234.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('3c0e9dfb-f542-5c9a-9f86-9cb7f01870ca','14ce2fb8-c99a-5fc2-9292-305f5a96b01b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','relating to the past',null,null,'تاریخی، مربوط به تاریخ؛ مهم از نظر تاریخ','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"places of historical interest","translation":"مکان های دیدنی تاریخی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001727051.mp3"},{"sentence":"It is important to look at the novel in its historical context .","translation":"نگاه کردن به رمان در بستر تاریخی آن بسیار مهم است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001727054.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('aa7cfe51-fcc4-531b-8ff3-9a2b449712ae','14ce2fb8-c99a-5fc2-9292-305f5a96b01b',2,null,null,'spoken & written','connected to the study of history',null,null,'مرتبط با مطالعه تاریخ','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('bb57cfda-8250-5b91-ac6d-36dc5326d3af','14ce2fb8-c99a-5fc2-9292-305f5a96b01b',3,null,null,'spoken & written','historical events , facts, people etc happened or existed in the past',null,null,'وقایع تاریخی، حقایق، مردم و غیره در گذشته اتفاق افتاده یا وجود داشته است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Was King Arthur a real historical figure?","translation":"آیا شاه آرتور یک شخصیت تاریخی واقعی بود؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001384988.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('a1b51859-0196-5591-8815-8aa76c3c3a41','14ce2fb8-c99a-5fc2-9292-305f5a96b01b',4,null,null,'spoken & written','describing or based on events in the past',null,null,'توصیف یا بر اساس رویدادهای گذشته','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a historical novel","translation":"یک رمان تاریخی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001384993.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('19b772ed-ae4b-5dae-9866-0ed24174f6ad','342258d4-3a6c-5e15-b79e-3ff602984452',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make the meaning of something clearer by giving examples',null,null,'تصویرسازی کردن؛ شرح دادن با مثال؛ شکل‌دار کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Let me give an example to illustrate the point .","translation":"بگذارید برای روشن شدن موضوع مثالی بزنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001401236.mp3"},{"sentence":"She illustrated her discussion with diagrams.","translation":"او بحث خود را با نمودارها نشان داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001750519.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('bcaa9a14-1bd1-5cc3-8351-e03e698b6e5b','342258d4-3a6c-5e15-b79e-3ff602984452',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to be an example which shows that something is true or that a fact exists',null,null,'مثالی باشد که نشان دهد چیزی درست است یا واقعیتی وجود دارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"This dispute illustrates that the regime is deeply divided.","translation":"این اختلاف نشان می دهد که رژیم عمیقاً دچار اختلاف شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001401240.mp3"},{"sentence":"The following examples illustrate how this operates in practice.","translation":"مثال‌های زیر نشان می‌دهند که این در عمل چگونه عمل می‌کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001750524.mp3"},{"sentence":"This illustrates a fundamental weakness in the system.","translation":"این یک ضعف اساسی در سیستم را نشان می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001750525.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('c118f705-3b43-5c85-8342-0b048a0da491','342258d4-3a6c-5e15-b79e-3ff602984452',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to put pictures in a book, article etc',null,null,'برای قرار دادن تصاویر در یک کتاب، مقاله و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Over a hundred diagrams, tables and pictures illustrate the book.","translation":"بیش از صد نمودار، جدول و تصویر کتاب را به تصویر می کشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001750526.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('04b0f3d5-357f-557c-a4d6-027ff3d2ba2a','6c32675d-e41a-5192-a125-1e3e54a8cb83',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the quality of being important',null,null,'اهمیت، اهمیت (روی)؛ قدر (شخص)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have importance This is an issue that has importance for all of us.','attach importance to something (= think it is important ) She attached great importance to loyalty.','recognize/realize the importance of something We all recognize the importance of his work.','emphasize/stress the importance of something I''d like to emphasize the importance of reading exam questions carefully.','assume importance (= become important ) The town assumed importance once it was connected to the rail system.','lose its importance The island lost its importance when trade routes changed.','exceed something in importance formal (= be more important than something else ) For him, winning Wimbledon exceeded all other tournaments in importance.','great/considerable/enormous importance Crime rates have great importance for the government. Some people attach enormous importance to personal wealth.','vital/crucial/critical importance (= very great ) This research is of vital importance.','central/fundamental importance The central importance of interest rates is widely recognized.','particular importance Tourism has particular importance in some regions.','equal importance When applying for a job, qualifications and experience are often of equal importance.','relative importance We discussed the relative importance of these different sources of revenue.','growing/increasing importance the growing importance of the Internet as a source of information','economic/political importance The role of the police has great political importance.','local/national importance Crime is an issue of national importance.','practical importance (= related to things that happen, rather than just ideas ) Science has long been of practical importance to civilization as a whole.','a sense/feeling of importance (= a feeling that you are an important person ) Sitting behind the big desk gave her a feeling of importance.','be of little/no importance Where the money came from is of no importance.','be of the utmost importance/be of paramount importance (= be extremely important ) It is of the utmost importance that this matter is kept confidential.','be of primary importance formal (= be the most important thing ) Finishing the project on time is of primary importance.','be of secondary importance formal (= be less important than another thing ) Sometimes we forget that the media coverage of a sport is actually of secondary importance to the event itself.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the importance of regular exercise","translation":"اهمیت ورزش منظم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001406974.mp3"},{"sentence":"I agree about the importance of these proposals (= the reasons why they are important ) .","translation":"من در مورد اهمیت این پیشنهادات (= دلایل مهم بودن آنها) موافقم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001709485.mp3"},{"sentence":"They make decisions about various matters of importance (= important matters ) .","translation":"آنها در مورد مسائل مختلف مهم (= مسائل مهم) تصمیم می گیرند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000826.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was full of his own importance (= he behaved in an annoying way which showed that he thought he was very important ) .","translation":"او از اهمیت خود پر بود (= رفتار آزاردهنده ای داشت که نشان می داد او را بسیار مهم می دانست) .","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa020100.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('973adf0e-3cae-5d6d-8744-04018ecce74c','5bbf6007-954b-5b25-9c94-e90d83bc30cb',1,null,null,'spoken & written','something that is impossible cannot happen or be done',null,null,'ناممکن، نمی‌شود؛ ناتمام (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['seem impossible It seemed impossible that he would ever recover from the injury.','become impossible As it became darker, it became impossible for the players to see the ball.','prove impossible (= be impossible because you have tried but not succeeded ) It proved impossible for the two sides to reach an agreement.','find something impossible He found it impossible to sleep because of the noise coming from next door.','make something impossible Heavy snow made travelling impossible.','render something impossible formal (= make something impossible ) The large number of prison guards rendered any escape impossible.','absolutely impossible ( also utterly impossible formal ) It is absolutely impossible to drive in these conditions.','almost/nearly impossible He thought that winning would be almost impossible.','virtually/practically impossible (= almost impossible ) Getting tickets for the concert is practically impossible.','well-nigh impossible formal (= almost impossible ) Policing the entire coastline is well-nigh impossible.','seemingly impossible (= seeming to be impossible ) He managed to win the chess game from a seemingly impossible position.','physically impossible It is physically impossible to survive for long in the desert without water.','an impossible job/task He faced the impossible task of paying back huge debts.','an impossible feat (= something that is impossible to do ) She achieved the seemingly impossible feat of breaking the world record.','an impossible dream (= something you want, but will never happen ) For a small club, winning the cup final will always be the impossible dream.','impossible demands She was growing tired of the company’s impossible demands.','it is impossible to do something It is impossible to know if this story is true.','difficult, if not impossible (= difficult, and perhaps impossible ) Obtaining funding for the film will be difficult, if not impossible.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘I want to speak to Mr Franks.’ ‘I’m afraid that’s impossible.’","translation":"«می‌خواهم با آقای فرانکز صحبت کنم.» «می‌ترسم این غیرممکن باشد.»","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972953.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s impossible to be accurate about these things.","translation":"نمی توان در مورد این موارد دقیق بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972954.mp3"},{"sentence":"The noise made sleep impossible .","translation":"سر و صدا خواب را غیرممکن می کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972957.mp3"},{"sentence":"Members with young children often found it impossible to attend evening meetings.","translation":"اعضای دارای فرزندان خردسال اغلب شرکت در جلسات عصر را غیرممکن می‌دانستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972963.mp3"},{"sentence":"It is difficult to find work these days, but for blind people it is virtually impossible .","translation":"این روزها یافتن کار دشوار است، اما برای افراد نابینا عملاً غیرممکن است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972967.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was faced with a seemingly impossible task.","translation":"او با یک کار به ظاهر غیرممکن روبرو بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972971.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was physically impossible to get the fridge through the door.","translation":"عبور یخچال از درب از نظر فیزیکی غیرممکن بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972975.mp3"},{"sentence":"Six months ago, peace seemed an impossible dream .","translation":"شش ماه پیش، صلح رویایی غیرممکن به نظر می رسید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972979.mp3"},{"sentence":"Such mental attitudes are difficult, if not impossible , to change.","translation":"تغییر چنین نگرش های ذهنی اگر غیرممکن نباشد، دشوار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972983.mp3"}]'::jsonb,9),
('cc4021c2-724a-5b96-a98f-7ff1c806ed7b','5bbf6007-954b-5b25-9c94-e90d83bc30cb',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a situation that is impossible is one that you cannot deal with',null,null,'موقعیتی که غیرممکن است موقعیتی است که نمی توانید با آن کنار بیایید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['seem impossible It seemed impossible that he would ever recover from the injury.','become impossible As it became darker, it became impossible for the players to see the ball.','prove impossible (= be impossible because you have tried but not succeeded ) It proved impossible for the two sides to reach an agreement.','find something impossible He found it impossible to sleep because of the noise coming from next door.','make something impossible Heavy snow made travelling impossible.','render something impossible formal (= make something impossible ) The large number of prison guards rendered any escape impossible.','absolutely impossible ( also utterly impossible formal ) It is absolutely impossible to drive in these conditions.','almost/nearly impossible He thought that winning would be almost impossible.','virtually/practically impossible (= almost impossible ) Getting tickets for the concert is practically impossible.','well-nigh impossible formal (= almost impossible ) Policing the entire coastline is well-nigh impossible.','seemingly impossible (= seeming to be impossible ) He managed to win the chess game from a seemingly impossible position.','physically impossible It is physically impossible to survive for long in the desert without water.','an impossible job/task He faced the impossible task of paying back huge debts.','an impossible feat (= something that is impossible to do ) She achieved the seemingly impossible feat of breaking the world record.','an impossible dream (= something you want, but will never happen ) For a small club, winning the cup final will always be the impossible dream.','impossible demands She was growing tired of the company’s impossible demands.','it is impossible to do something It is impossible to know if this story is true.','difficult, if not impossible (= difficult, and perhaps impossible ) Obtaining funding for the film will be difficult, if not impossible.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We were in an impossible situation. Whatever we decided to do would upset someone.","translation":"در شرایط غیرممکنی قرار داشتیم. هر کاری که تصمیم می گرفتیم انجام دهیم باعث ناراحتی کسی می شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001709575.mp3"},{"sentence":"Helen’s refusal to cooperate put me in an impossible position .","translation":"امتناع هلن از همکاری مرا در موقعیتی ناممکن قرار داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001407990.mp3"},{"sentence":"His attitude is making life impossible for the rest of the team.","translation":"نگرش او زندگی را برای بقیه اعضای تیم غیرممکن می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001407991.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was facing impossible odds.","translation":"او با مشکلات غیرممکن روبرو بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001709584.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('645ddeac-323f-5705-b0f5-cbfcbd3e2fae','5bbf6007-954b-5b25-9c94-e90d83bc30cb',3,null,null,'spoken & written','behaving in a very unreasonable and annoying way',null,null,'رفتار بسیار غیر منطقی و آزاردهنده','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['seem impossible It seemed impossible that he would ever recover from the injury.','become impossible As it became darker, it became impossible for the players to see the ball.','prove impossible (= be impossible because you have tried but not succeeded ) It proved impossible for the two sides to reach an agreement.','find something impossible He found it impossible to sleep because of the noise coming from next door.','make something impossible Heavy snow made travelling impossible.','render something impossible formal (= make something impossible ) The large number of prison guards rendered any escape impossible.','absolutely impossible ( also utterly impossible formal ) It is absolutely impossible to drive in these conditions.','almost/nearly impossible He thought that winning would be almost impossible.','virtually/practically impossible (= almost impossible ) Getting tickets for the concert is practically impossible.','well-nigh impossible formal (= almost impossible ) Policing the entire coastline is well-nigh impossible.','seemingly impossible (= seeming to be impossible ) He managed to win the chess game from a seemingly impossible position.','physically impossible It is physically impossible to survive for long in the desert without water.','an impossible job/task He faced the impossible task of paying back huge debts.','an impossible feat (= something that is impossible to do ) She achieved the seemingly impossible feat of breaking the world record.','an impossible dream (= something you want, but will never happen ) For a small club, winning the cup final will always be the impossible dream.','impossible demands She was growing tired of the company’s impossible demands.','it is impossible to do something It is impossible to know if this story is true.','difficult, if not impossible (= difficult, and perhaps impossible ) Obtaining funding for the film will be difficult, if not impossible.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Oh, you’re just impossible!","translation":"اوه، تو غیرممکنی!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001407996.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('322a65f7-98ce-557c-b324-c05d6ffcc922','df7c9a1a-2b0c-587e-b01b-579fc4610dc2',1,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'the impossible',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('aa87a695-8a4f-5f64-ac47-4fcfe29ee980','908cf14a-f36b-566a-8f35-d3ac55c1074a',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the opinion or feeling you have about someone or something because of the way they seem','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'برداشت، تأثیر؛ قالب (ماشین)؛ قالب (ریختن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make an impression Think about what sort of impression you want to make.','give an impression Her speech definitely gave the impression that she was enthusiastic about the project.','create an impression ( also convey an impression formal ) Arriving late won’t create a very good impression.','get an impression What sort of impression did you get of the city?','leave an impression on somebody (= make someone remember a person, place, or thing ) Janet certainly left an impression on him.','a good/positive impression He was keen to make a good impression on his boss.','a bad/negative impression Arriving late for an interview gives a very negative impression.','somebody’s first/initial/immediate impression My first impression was that Terry’s version of the events was untrue.','a clear/vivid impression He had the clear impression that most people were in favour of the idea.','a vague impression (= not very clear ) Dave only had a vague impression of the man who had attacked him.','a strong/deep impression (= one that someone feels very strongly ) She made a strong impression on me the first time I met her.','a lasting impression (= one that someone remembers for a long time ) Sam’s performance had clearly made a lasting impression on the audience.','the overwhelming/overriding impression (= an impression that is stronger than all others ) The overwhelming impression after the meeting was one of optimism.','an indelible impression formal (= lasting for ever ) Alan’s wartime experiences had left an indelible impression on him.','a wrong/misleading impression The advertisement gave a misleading impression of the product.','a false/mistaken impression He had the mistaken impression that Julia was married. Many people got the false impression she didn’t care.','the overall/general impression The general impression was of a very efficiently run company.','the distinct impression (= used when something seems very clear to you ) We were left with the impression that the contract was ours if we wanted it.','somebody’s personal impression My personal impression is that the new manager has greatly improved things.','first impressions count (= the impression you make when you first meet someone is important ) When attending a job interview, remember that first impressions count.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"When we looked around the school we got a very good impression.","translation":"وقتی اطراف مدرسه را نگاه کردیم، برداشت بسیار خوبی داشتیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000828.mp3"},{"sentence":"I got the impression that she wasn''t very happy with her job.","translation":"این تصور را داشتم که او از کارش چندان راضی نیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040098.mp3"},{"sentence":"What was your impression of Roger?","translation":"برداشت شما از راجر چه بود؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000829.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('7b31ee97-cff9-54ba-aeb9-943167bfcea1','908cf14a-f36b-566a-8f35-d3ac55c1074a',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be under the impression (that)','برداشت، تأثیر؛ قالب (ماشین)؛ قالب (ریختن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make an impression Think about what sort of impression you want to make.','give an impression Her speech definitely gave the impression that she was enthusiastic about the project.','create an impression ( also convey an impression formal ) Arriving late won’t create a very good impression.','get an impression What sort of impression did you get of the city?','leave an impression on somebody (= make someone remember a person, place, or thing ) Janet certainly left an impression on him.','a good/positive impression He was keen to make a good impression on his boss.','a bad/negative impression Arriving late for an interview gives a very negative impression.','somebody’s first/initial/immediate impression My first impression was that Terry’s version of the events was untrue.','a clear/vivid impression He had the clear impression that most people were in favour of the idea.','a vague impression (= not very clear ) Dave only had a vague impression of the man who had attacked him.','a strong/deep impression (= one that someone feels very strongly ) She made a strong impression on me the first time I met her.','a lasting impression (= one that someone remembers for a long time ) Sam’s performance had clearly made a lasting impression on the audience.','the overwhelming/overriding impression (= an impression that is stronger than all others ) The overwhelming impression after the meeting was one of optimism.','an indelible impression formal (= lasting for ever ) Alan’s wartime experiences had left an indelible impression on him.','a wrong/misleading impression The advertisement gave a misleading impression of the product.','a false/mistaken impression He had the mistaken impression that Julia was married. Many people got the false impression she didn’t care.','the overall/general impression The general impression was of a very efficiently run company.','the distinct impression (= used when something seems very clear to you ) We were left with the impression that the contract was ours if we wanted it.','somebody’s personal impression My personal impression is that the new manager has greatly improved things.','first impressions count (= the impression you make when you first meet someone is important ) When attending a job interview, remember that first impressions count.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('0dc9d892-c4d7-54d4-bce3-b843d7573297','908cf14a-f36b-566a-8f35-d3ac55c1074a',3,null,null,'spoken & written','if you do an impression of a famous person, you copy their speech or behaviour in order to make people laugh','[ countable ]',null,'اگر تصوری از یک فرد مشهور داشته باشید، گفتار یا رفتار او را کپی می کنید تا مردم را بخندانید',array['imitation']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make an impression Think about what sort of impression you want to make.','give an impression Her speech definitely gave the impression that she was enthusiastic about the project.','create an impression ( also convey an impression formal ) Arriving late won’t create a very good impression.','get an impression What sort of impression did you get of the city?','leave an impression on somebody (= make someone remember a person, place, or thing ) Janet certainly left an impression on him.','a good/positive impression He was keen to make a good impression on his boss.','a bad/negative impression Arriving late for an interview gives a very negative impression.','somebody’s first/initial/immediate impression My first impression was that Terry’s version of the events was untrue.','a clear/vivid impression He had the clear impression that most people were in favour of the idea.','a vague impression (= not very clear ) Dave only had a vague impression of the man who had attacked him.','a strong/deep impression (= one that someone feels very strongly ) She made a strong impression on me the first time I met her.','a lasting impression (= one that someone remembers for a long time ) Sam’s performance had clearly made a lasting impression on the audience.','the overwhelming/overriding impression (= an impression that is stronger than all others ) The overwhelming impression after the meeting was one of optimism.','an indelible impression formal (= lasting for ever ) Alan’s wartime experiences had left an indelible impression on him.','a wrong/misleading impression The advertisement gave a misleading impression of the product.','a false/mistaken impression He had the mistaken impression that Julia was married. Many people got the false impression she didn’t care.','the overall/general impression The general impression was of a very efficiently run company.','the distinct impression (= used when something seems very clear to you ) We were left with the impression that the contract was ours if we wanted it.','somebody’s personal impression My personal impression is that the new manager has greatly improved things.','first impressions count (= the impression you make when you first meet someone is important ) When attending a job interview, remember that first impressions count.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Jean does a great impression of Madonna.","translation":"ژان تاثیر بسیار خوبی از مدونا می گذارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001408664.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('8ba23680-40c1-5c1d-baec-29043b2af514','908cf14a-f36b-566a-8f35-d3ac55c1074a',4,null,null,'spoken & written','a picture or drawing of what someone or something might look like, or what something will look like in the future','[ countable ]',null,'تصویر یا نقاشی از اینکه ممکن است کسی یا چیزی شبیه به چه چیزی باشد یا چیزی در آینده چگونه باشد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make an impression Think about what sort of impression you want to make.','give an impression Her speech definitely gave the impression that she was enthusiastic about the project.','create an impression ( also convey an impression formal ) Arriving late won’t create a very good impression.','get an impression What sort of impression did you get of the city?','leave an impression on somebody (= make someone remember a person, place, or thing ) Janet certainly left an impression on him.','a good/positive impression He was keen to make a good impression on his boss.','a bad/negative impression Arriving late for an interview gives a very negative impression.','somebody’s first/initial/immediate impression My first impression was that Terry’s version of the events was untrue.','a clear/vivid impression He had the clear impression that most people were in favour of the idea.','a vague impression (= not very clear ) Dave only had a vague impression of the man who had attacked him.','a strong/deep impression (= one that someone feels very strongly ) She made a strong impression on me the first time I met her.','a lasting impression (= one that someone remembers for a long time ) Sam’s performance had clearly made a lasting impression on the audience.','the overwhelming/overriding impression (= an impression that is stronger than all others ) The overwhelming impression after the meeting was one of optimism.','an indelible impression formal (= lasting for ever ) Alan’s wartime experiences had left an indelible impression on him.','a wrong/misleading impression The advertisement gave a misleading impressio