sition/arouse the opposition of somebody (= make someone feel disagreement ) A plan to build on farm land aroused local opposition.','opposition comes from somebody The strongest opposition came from Republican voters.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('2ff54b90-c701-512f-8937-427ccb9883d1','822ea396-a34e-50cf-a8c6-e3d9d6d3414d',4,null,null,'spoken & written','the people who you are competing against','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'افرادی که با آنها رقابت می کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['strong opposition (= disagreement that someone feels strongly ) The scheme has met with strong opposition from local people.','fierce/intense/stiff opposition (= strong opposition ) It is certain that there will be fierce opposition to the changes.','violent/vehement opposition (= showing extremely strong angry feelings ) The 2,000-strong congress met the violent opposition of left-wingers. There has been vehement opposition from the fishing industry.','considerable opposition (= quite a lot of opposition ) The development went ahead in spite of considerable opposition.','growing/mounting opposition (= opposition that is increasing ) There was growing opposition to the war.','local opposition It took three years to overcome local opposition from environmentalists.','widespread opposition (= opposition from many people or in many places ) Journalists have reported widespread opposition to the regime.','public opposition Public opposition has blocked the building of nuclear power stations.','organized opposition (= protest that people express by working together in an organized way ) The proposal was passed with no organized opposition.','face opposition (= experience opposition that has to be dealt with ) The proposal faced opposition from road safety campaigners.','meet (with) opposition/run into opposition (= face opposition ) A new tax would meet a lot of opposition. The Bill ran into opposition in the House of Lords.','encounter opposition (= find that there is opposition ) The police encountered little opposition, and restored order within the hour.','express (your) opposition Parents expressed their opposition to the tests.','overcome opposition (= deal with opposition so that it no longer exists ) Nothing he said could overcome their opposition.','arouse opposition/arouse the opposition of somebody (= make someone feel disagreement ) A plan to build on farm land aroused local opposition.','opposition comes from somebody The strongest opposition came from Republican voters.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"They played well against good opposition.","translation":"آنها مقابل حریفان خوب بازی کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001578330.mp3"},{"sentence":"The opposition was too strong for us.","translation":"اپوزیسیون برای ما خیلی قوی بود.","audio_url":null},{"sentence":"The opposition were too strong for us.","translation":"مخالفان برای ما خیلی قوی بودند.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,3),
('2fcad2a0-df97-5e89-b7cd-80b91684257a','822ea396-a34e-50cf-a8c6-e3d9d6d3414d',5,null,null,'formal','when two things are completely opposite','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'وقتی دو چیز کاملاً متضاد هستند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['strong opposition (= disagreement that someone feels strongly ) The scheme has met with strong opposition from local people.','fierce/intense/stiff opposition (= strong opposition ) It is certain that there will be fierce opposition to the changes.','violent/vehement opposition (= showing extremely strong angry feelings ) The 2,000-strong congress met the violent opposition of left-wingers. There has been vehement opposition from the fishing industry.','considerable opposition (= quite a lot of opposition ) The development went ahead in spite of considerable opposition.','growing/mounting opposition (= opposition that is increasing ) There was growing opposition to the war.','local opposition It took three years to overcome local opposition from environmentalists.','widespread opposition (= opposition from many people or in many places ) Journalists have reported widespread opposition to the regime.','public opposition Public opposition has blocked the building of nuclear power stations.','organized opposition (= protest that people express by working together in an organized way ) The proposal was passed with no organized opposition.','face opposition (= experience opposition that has to be dealt with ) The proposal faced opposition from road safety campaigners.','meet (with) opposition/run into opposition (= face opposition ) A new tax would meet a lot of opposition. The Bill ran into opposition in the House of Lords.','encounter opposition (= find that there is opposition ) The police encountered little opposition, and restored order within the hour.','express (your) opposition Parents expressed their opposition to the tests.','overcome opposition (= deal with opposition so that it no longer exists ) Nothing he said could overcome their opposition.','arouse opposition/arouse the opposition of somebody (= make someone feel disagreement ) A plan to build on farm land aroused local opposition.','opposition comes from somebody The strongest opposition came from Republican voters.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the opposition between capitalism and socialism","translation":"تقابل سرمایه داری و سوسیالیسم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001578337.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('bef3ddb0-cc9d-593e-949d-1e3716381fdb','c1f03569-cb1a-5ae6-81a3-3534488fa583',1,null,null,'spoken & written','in the beginning, before other things happened or before things changed','[ sentence adverb ]',null,'در آغاز، ابتدا؛ اصل (نظر)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The family originally came from France.","translation":"این خانواده در اصل اهل فرانسه بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000380128.mp3"},{"sentence":"The building was originally used as a prison.","translation":"این ساختمان در ابتدا به عنوان زندان مورد استفاده قرار می گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000380129.mp3"},{"sentence":"We originally intended to stay for just a few days.","translation":"ما در ابتدا قصد داشتیم فقط چند روز بمانیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001567156.mp3"},{"sentence":"Originally, we had planned a tour of Scotland but we didn’t go in the end.","translation":"در ابتدا، ما یک تور اسکاتلند را برنامه ریزی کرده بودیم اما در نهایت نرفتیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000380132.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('0981c7b8-470b-5c26-b48b-5ff25524dd22','03f1a83a-179e-52cc-bdf6-ac0150814b3c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the group of people who are elected to make a country’s laws and discuss important national affairs','[ countable ]',null,'پارلمان، مجلس (قانون‌گذاری)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be elected to parliament She was elected to parliament in 1997.','stand for parliament (= try to be elected ) Ms Jackson stood for Parliament as a Labour candidate.','enter/get into parliament (= be elected as a member of parliament ) Tony Blair first entered Parliament in 1983.','be returned to Parliament (= be elected ) Creevey was returned to Parliament as MP for Appleby.','a bill is passed by parliament (= it is made into a law ) The bill was passed by Parliament last May.','a bill goes through parliament (= it goes through the process of being made a law ) The bill is currently going through Parliament.','go before/be put before parliament (= be considered by parliament ) The Bill goes before Parliament on November 16.','dissolve parliament formal (= officially end parliament before holding an election ) The prime minister will ask the Queen to dissolve Parliament and call an election.','a member of parliament He was the Conservative member of Parliament for Edgbaston.','an act of parliament (= a law that has been passed by parliament ) Their rights are guaranteed by Act of Parliament.','a seat in parliament (= a position as member of parliament ) If Morgan resigns his seat in Parliament, there will be a bye-election.','a session of parliament (= when its members are working ) The Queen opened a new session of Parliament last week.','the lifetime of a parliament (= from when a government is elected until it calls an election ) We shall not make changes in this area, at least in the lifetime of this Parliament.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"They demanded a free parliament and press.","translation":"آنها خواستار پارلمان و مطبوعات آزاد شدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001167.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('da8edec7-911b-5c1a-9be0-4f241854bbda','03f1a83a-179e-52cc-bdf6-ac0150814b3c',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'Parliament','پارلمان، مجلس (قانون‌گذاری)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be elected to parliament She was elected to parliament in 1997.','stand for parliament (= try to be elected ) Ms Jackson stood for Parliament as a Labour candidate.','enter/get into parliament (= be elected as a member of parliament ) Tony Blair first entered Parliament in 1983.','be returned to Parliament (= be elected ) Creevey was returned to Parliament as MP for Appleby.','a bill is passed by parliament (= it is made into a law ) The bill was passed by Parliament last May.','a bill goes through parliament (= it goes through the process of being made a law ) The bill is currently going through Parliament.','go before/be put before parliament (= be considered by parliament ) The Bill goes before Parliament on November 16.','dissolve parliament formal (= officially end parliament before holding an election ) The prime minister will ask the Queen to dissolve Parliament and call an election.','a member of parliament He was the Conservative member of Parliament for Edgbaston.','an act of parliament (= a law that has been passed by parliament ) Their rights are guaranteed by Act of Parliament.','a seat in parliament (= a position as member of parliament ) If Morgan resigns his seat in Parliament, there will be a bye-election.','a session of parliament (= when its members are working ) The Queen opened a new session of Parliament last week.','the lifetime of a parliament (= from when a government is elected until it calls an election ) We shall not make changes in this area, at least in the lifetime of this Parliament.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('5fe3f7f1-f640-5363-8013-e53266b83b27','03f1a83a-179e-52cc-bdf6-ac0150814b3c',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the period during which the British Parliament meets','[ countable ]',null,'دوره ای که در آن پارلمان بریتانیا تشکیل جلسه می دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We expect to get these laws passed during the present parliament.","translation":"ما انتظار داریم این قوانین در مجلس فعلی به تصویب برسد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000366402.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('4824fc4c-67f6-5cbc-96cc-f094b6051c69','19bbe808-f821-5d42-8790-035b67e5da08',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the main law-making institution in the UK, which consists of the House of Commons and the House of Lords',null,'hung parliament','اصلی ترین نهاد قانونگذار در بریتانیا که از مجلس عوام و مجلس اعیان تشکیل شده است.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The government has actually increased its majority in Parliament.","translation":"دولت در واقع اکثریت خود را در مجلس افزایش داده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001168.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('94412003-64c8-523b-a682-5b18db360e8e','d43b4b72-4a7c-5755-9ed2-e52a4eb04519',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a particular thing or person is the one that you are talking about, and not any other','[ only before noun ]',null,'خاص، ویژه؛ معین (مورد)؛ مواظب (بیشتر دقت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"In this particular case, no one else was involved.","translation":"در این مورد خاص، شخص دیگری درگیر نبود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000368110.mp3"},{"sentence":"Most students choose one particular area for research.","translation":"اکثر دانش آموزان یک حوزه خاص را برای تحقیق انتخاب می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000368111.mp3"},{"sentence":"a particular type of food","translation":"نوع خاصی از غذا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001559022.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('4561ed6a-31b0-5eb9-93c1-be9ccb564cba','d43b4b72-4a7c-5755-9ed2-e52a4eb04519',2,null,null,'spoken & written','special or great',null,null,'خاص یا عالی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"You should pay particular attention to spelling.","translation":"شما باید به املا توجه خاصی داشته باشید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000368115.mp3"},{"sentence":"For no particular reason , he quit the job.","translation":"بدون هیچ دلیل خاصی از این کار کناره گیری کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000368117.mp3"},{"sentence":"Of particular concern is the rising cost of transportation.","translation":"نگرانی ویژه افزایش هزینه حمل و نقل است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001559034.mp3"},{"sentence":"I had nothing particular planned.","translation":"برنامه خاصی نداشتم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001559037.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('2ddbd952-e0ec-5820-bebd-7ad49cedc47b','d43b4b72-4a7c-5755-9ed2-e52a4eb04519',3,null,null,'spoken & written','very careful about choosing exactly what you like and not easily satisfied',null,null,'در انتخاب دقیقاً چیزی که دوست دارید بسیار مراقب باشید و به راحتی راضی نمی شوید',array['fussy']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Marty’s very particular about his food.","translation":"مارتی در مورد غذایش بسیار خاص است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000368123.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('d46a1f28-249e-5bd7-8859-ac218764d12c','278e0a40-8972-512c-9941-c458ca8ec021',1,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'in particular',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('1df56b45-e5f8-5217-9aee-9f194f68823c','278e0a40-8972-512c-9941-c458ca8ec021',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'particulars',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('861cfe1c-796e-57a5-a91b-1455844fa474','278e0a40-8972-512c-9941-c458ca8ec021',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'in every particular/in all particulars',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('83963f2c-d1bc-5146-b63e-0b9c07ed3ff1','468e422d-c722-585d-b68c-31879ec23405',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an amount expressed as if it is part of a total which is 100','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'درصد، نسبت (درصدی)؛ درصد (مالی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['high/large A high percentage of our students pass the exam.','small/low Only a small percentage of people suffer from the allergy.','significant We get a significant percentage of our oil from Nigeria and Angola.','a percentage point (= one percent ) The party increased its share of the vote by almost 4 percentage points.','a percentage increase/change Poorer pensioners experienced the greatest percentage increase in their pensions.','in percentage terms The quantity of carbon dioxide was, in percentage terms, extremely small.','express something as a percentage The number is expressed as a percentage of the total population of the country.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The percentage of school leavers that go to university is about five per cent.","translation":"درصد ترک تحصیلی که به دانشگاه می روند حدود پنج درصد است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000349582.mp3"},{"sentence":"Tax is paid as a percentage of total income.","translation":"مالیات به عنوان درصدی از کل درآمد پرداخت می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001537815.mp3"},{"sentence":"A high percentage of married women have part-time jobs.","translation":"درصد بالایی از زنان متاهل دارای مشاغل پاره وقت هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000349585.mp3"},{"sentence":"Interest rates fell by six percentage points (= 6% ) .","translation":"نرخ بهره شش درصد کاهش یافت (= 6%).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001765797.mp3"},{"sentence":"The numbers are small in percentage terms (= when calculated as a percentage ) .","translation":"اعداد از نظر درصد کوچک هستند (= وقتی به صورت درصد محاسبه می شوند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001765802.mp3"},{"sentence":"Crime figures showed significant percentage increases.","translation":"ارقام جرم درصد افزایش قابل توجهی را نشان می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001765807.mp3"},{"sentence":"Only a small percentage of people are interested in politics.","translation":"تنها درصد کمی از مردم به سیاست علاقه دارند.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,7),
('7737973e-7aaf-51da-998e-3250dd34d127','468e422d-c722-585d-b68c-31879ec23405',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a share of the profits','[ countable usually singular ]',null,'سهمی از سود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['high/large A high percentage of our students pass the exam.','small/low Only a small percentage of people suffer from the allergy.','significant We get a significant percentage of our oil from Nigeria and Angola.','a percentage point (= one percent ) The party increased its share of the vote by almost 4 percentage points.','a percentage increase/change Poorer pensioners experienced the greatest percentage increase in their pensions.','in percentage terms The quantity of carbon dioxide was, in percentage terms, extremely small.','express something as a percentage The number is expressed as a percentage of the total population of the country.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She gets a percentage for every record sold.","translation":"او به ازای هر رکورد فروخته شده درصدی دریافت می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000349593.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('80060e48-3392-5ad6-8060-46fb048bdc71','468e422d-c722-585d-b68c-31879ec23405',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'there is no percentage in doing something','درصد، نسبت (درصدی)؛ درصد (مالی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['high/large A high percentage of our students pass the exam.','small/low Only a small percentage of people suffer from the allergy.','significant We get a significant percentage of our oil from Nigeria and Angola.','a percentage point (= one percent ) The party increased its share of the vote by almost 4 percentage points.','a percentage increase/change Poorer pensioners experienced the greatest percentage increase in their pensions.','in percentage terms The quantity of carbon dioxide was, in percentage terms, extremely small.','express something as a percentage The number is expressed as a percentage of the total population of the country.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('478c8e2d-ff85-598f-9c39-81bcf7abc20e','1400ff9e-fad5-5617-93ba-745458b01f33',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the way you think about something and your idea of what it is like','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'ادراک، ادراک‌کردن (ذهنی)؛ برداشت؛ ادراک (حسی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"children’s perceptions of the world","translation":"درک کودکان از جهان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000349629.mp3"},{"sentence":"the public perception of the government’s performance","translation":"درک عمومی از عملکرد دولت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001537835.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('cc224e4b-2510-5030-86c5-60abd09708c2','1400ff9e-fad5-5617-93ba-745458b01f33',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the way that you notice things with your senses of sight , hearing etc','[ uncountable ]',null,'روشی که با حواس بینایی، شنوایی و غیره متوجه چیزها می شوید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"drugs that alter perception","translation":"داروهایی که ادراک را تغییر می دهند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000349634.mp3"},{"sentence":"visual perception","translation":"ادراک بصری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001765809.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('ea0a3b92-adff-5294-beb8-4ee48be597fc','1400ff9e-fad5-5617-93ba-745458b01f33',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the natural ability to understand or notice things quickly','[ uncountable ]',null,'توانایی طبیعی برای درک یا تشخیص سریع چیزها','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Ross shows unusual perception for a boy of his age.","translation":"راس برای پسری هم سن و سال خود درک غیرعادی نشان می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000349639.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('061cca7b-2bb5-5b12-b1d2-2b1bfb030a3c','b2491d1e-4cde-51d3-882e-d0f491152d82',1,null,null,'spoken & written','if you have permission to do something, you are officially allowed to do it',null,null,'اجازه، رخصت؛ اجازه رسمی (پدر)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have permission to do something They did not have permission to build on the land.','ask (for) permission ( also request permission formal ) Tommy asked for permission to go to the bathroom. Captain Miller requested permission to land.','apply for permission (= ask for official written permission ) The company has applied for permission to drill for oil.','get permission ( also obtain/receive permission formal ) We''ll need to get permission to film in the museum. You must obtain permission from the owners before viewing the property.','give permission ( also grant somebody permission formal ) The city authorities gave permission for the rally to take place. In 1961, he was granted permission to emigrate to Israel.','refuse/deny (somebody) permission Betty''s father refused her permission to attend the dance.','seek permission formal (= ask someone for permission ) People wanting to visit the island have to seek permission from the authorities.','need permission You''ll need written permission from your parents first.','written permission Doctors need written permission from the patient before they can operate.','special permission The paintings cannot be taken out of Russia without special permission.','official permission Mr Murphy was granted official permission to travel to North Korea.','planning permission (= official permission to build a new building or change an existing one ) The bank has applied for planning permission to redevelop a 1¼-acre site.','express permission (= definitely or clearly given ) He is not to leave without my express permission.','without permission Pages should not be copied without the permission of the publisher.','with somebody''s permission With your permission, I''d like to talk to your son alone.','by kind permission of somebody formal (= used for thanking someone for allowing something ) This photograph is reproduced by kind permission of Country Living.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"You''ll have to get permission from your parents if you want to come.","translation":"اگر می خواهید بیایید باید از والدینتان اجازه بگیرید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001189.mp3"},{"sentence":"The Council refused permission for the development.","translation":"شورا اجازه توسعه را رد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001190.mp3"},{"sentence":"Photographs should only be taken with the permission of the subject.","translation":"عکس ها فقط باید با اجازه سوژه گرفته شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00646.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('a4ed2cd3-a866-5a00-9860-dffa7fdd8afb','30f4fcce-c34d-5de0-84bc-09e13e270112',1,null,null,'spoken','used to emphasize that you are only giving your own opinion about something','[ sentence adverb ]',null,'به‌طور شخصی، خودم (نظر)؛ شخصاً','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Personally, I don’t think much of the idea.","translation":"من شخصاً به این ایده فکر نمی کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000353406.mp3"},{"sentence":"I personally think it’s too cold to go out.","translation":"من شخصا فکر می کنم برای بیرون رفتن خیلی سرد است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001584573.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('e7022340-2f35-5e12-8aa2-78af9ca0fcff','30f4fcce-c34d-5de0-84bc-09e13e270112',2,null,null,'spoken & written','if you do something personally, you do it yourself rather than getting someone else to do it',null,null,'اگر کاری را شخصا انجام می دهید، به جای اینکه شخص دیگری را مجبور به انجام آن کنید، آن را خودتان انجام می دهید',array['in person']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The managing director wrote personally to thank me.","translation":"مدیر عامل شخصا برای تشکر از من نوشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000353412.mp3"},{"sentence":"All important work is personally approved by him.","translation":"تمام کارهای مهم شخصاً توسط او تأیید می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001584574.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’ll see to it personally.","translation":"من شخصاً به آن رسیدگی خواهم کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001584575.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('803592fe-57c2-5ac3-b70d-bf1d9021e833','30f4fcce-c34d-5de0-84bc-09e13e270112',3,null,null,'spoken & written','used to show that one particular person is involved, rather than a group of people',null,null,'برای نشان دادن اینکه یک شخص خاص به جای گروهی از افراد درگیر است استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’m holding you personally responsible for this mess!","translation":"من شخصاً شما را مسئول این آشفتگی می دانم!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000353411.mp3"},{"sentence":"She clearly blamed me personally for the difficulties she’d been having.","translation":"او به وضوح شخصاً من را به خاطر مشکلاتی که داشت سرزنش کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001584583.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('478af172-9fbc-5bfa-9b5d-ba06e2a6a267','30f4fcce-c34d-5de0-84bc-09e13e270112',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'take something personally','به‌طور شخصی، خودم (نظر)؛ شخصاً','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('6dbea50f-236d-5b12-a0d6-c054485330b8','30f4fcce-c34d-5de0-84bc-09e13e270112',5,null,null,'spoken & written','as a friend , or as someone you have met',null,null,'به عنوان یک دوست، یا به عنوان کسی که ملاقات کرده اید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I don’t know her personally , but I like her work.","translation":"من شخصاً او را نمی شناسم، اما کار او را دوست دارم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000353427.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('5824db10-2d4e-52bb-b792-93843c3d807e','30f4fcce-c34d-5de0-84bc-09e13e270112',6,null,null,'spoken & written','in a way that criticizes someone’s character or appearance',null,null,'به نحوی که شخصیت یا ظاهر کسی را مورد انتقاد قرار دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Members of the Senate rarely attack each other personally.","translation":"اعضای سنا به ندرت شخصاً به یکدیگر حمله می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000353422.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('273481bf-57f8-5e99-84c3-e78ef3f264ad','30f4fcce-c34d-5de0-84bc-09e13e270112',7,null,null,'spoken & written','in relation to someone’s private life, rather than to their work, business, or official duties',null,null,'در رابطه با زندگی خصوصی یک فرد، به جای کار، تجارت یا وظایف رسمی او','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She had a lasting impact on his life both personally and professionally.","translation":"او تأثیر ماندگاری بر زندگی او چه از نظر شخصی و چه از نظر حرفه ای داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001584591.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c6b1e584-b705-5fbe-8fe4-73b91377ea54','45654bb4-f38a-5188-b2b5-f47fcf81f3fc',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the study of the nature and meaning of existence , truth , good and evil etc','[ uncountable ]',null,'فلسفه، حکمت؛ طرز تفکر؛ اصل (شرکت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Emma studies philosophy at university.","translation":"اما در دانشگاه فلسفه می خواند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566078.mp3"},{"sentence":"the philosophy of science","translation":"فلسفه علم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566077.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('dcecee71-c876-5649-98fe-72b8212b6e03','45654bb4-f38a-5188-b2b5-f47fcf81f3fc',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the views of a particular philosopher or group of philosophers','[ countable ]',null,'نظرات یک فیلسوف خاص یا گروهی از فیلسوفان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the philosophy of Aristotle","translation":"فلسفه ارسطو","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566082.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('0942fd9a-095b-5503-9700-67e52f83e03a','45654bb4-f38a-5188-b2b5-f47fcf81f3fc',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the attitude or set of ideas that guides the behaviour of a person or organization','[ countable ]',null,'نگرش یا مجموعه ایده هایی که رفتار یک فرد یا سازمان را هدایت می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The company explained their management philosophy.","translation":"این شرکت فلسفه مدیریت خود را توضیح داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000356166.mp3"},{"sentence":"The idea that you should treat others as you would like them to treat you is a fine philosophy of life .","translation":"این ایده که باید با دیگران همانطور رفتار کنید که دوست دارید با شما رفتار کنند، فلسفه خوبی از زندگی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566087.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('fc445385-8faf-5727-ba1c-52b2a5f58f4d','9a9cae65-942c-5c8f-9318-e761ca3fa44f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a picture obtained by using a camera and film that is sensitive to light',null,null,'عکس، تصویر (کامرا)؛ عکس‌گرفتگی (عکس)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['take a photograph He wanted to take a photograph of me.','get a photograph (= take one successfully ) I got some brilliant photographs of the desert.','a colour photograph The book is fully illustrated with colour photographs.','a black-and-white photograph','a digital photograph','a framed photograph On the desk was a framed photograph of a woman.','a signed photograph He keeps a signed photograph of Bill Clinton in his office.','a wedding photograph Your wedding photographs will keep the memories of the big day alive for you.','an aerial photograph (= one taken from a plane ) Aerial photographs can be used to locate archaeological sites.','faded All her life she kept a faded photograph of him in his army uniform.','blurred He was shown a blurred photograph, taken from a moving car.','grainy (= with a rough, not sharp, appearance ) I stared at the grainy newspaper photograph, searching for my mother.','sepia (= used about a black and white photograph that has shades of brown, in a way that is typical of old photographs ) an 1854 sepia photograph of Jonathan Pickering, the company founder','a photograph album (= a book in which you put photographs ) Mama kept a photograph album full of pictures of her family.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a colour photograph","translation":"یک عکس رنگی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000357402.mp3"},{"sentence":"a black and white photograph","translation":"یک عکس سیاه و سفید","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566206.mp3"},{"sentence":"I wish I had a photograph of Thomas.","translation":"کاش عکسی از توماس داشتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566214.mp3"},{"sentence":"He took a photograph of the hotel.","translation":"از هتل عکس گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566215.mp3"},{"sentence":"Tim was looking through an old photograph album (= book in which you put photographs ) .","translation":"تیم داشت از طریق یک آلبوم عکس قدیمی (= کتابی که در آن عکس می گذارید) نگاه می کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566209.mp3"},{"sentence":"Did you see Leo’s photograph (= a photograph of Leo ) in the newspaper?","translation":"آیا عکس لئو (= عکس لئو) را در روزنامه دیدید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001768823.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('985713ac-178e-5922-85c0-800436812d9f','e9947816-e9ba-5d87-8cfe-67d1927feccc',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to take a photograph of someone or something','[ transitive ]',null,'از کسی یا چیزی عکس گرفتن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Kate agreed to let me photograph her.","translation":"کیت قبول کرد که از او عکس بگیرم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000357422.mp3"},{"sentence":"He stood by the tree to be photographed.","translation":"کنار درخت ایستاد تا از او عکس بگیرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566221.mp3"},{"sentence":"She agreed to let me take her photo .","translation":"او قبول کرد که من عکسش را بگیرم.","audio_url":null},{"sentence":"He stood there waiting to have his picture taken .","translation":"او آنجا ایستاده بود و منتظر بود تا عکسش را بگیرند.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,4),
('666dc282-216e-5c59-a6a1-a03de2e8a847','e9947816-e9ba-5d87-8cfe-67d1927feccc',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'photograph well',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('50d7dfce-2ef7-5798-8445-026c6b4dc355','7593498d-7d3c-5eb8-ae01-ef762c65336d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','in relation to your body rather than your mind or emotions',null,null,'به‌طور بدنی، جسمی؛ از نظر فیزیکی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['physically fit It is important to keep yourself physically fit.','physically active He remained physically active far into old age.','physically disabled The attack left her physically disabled.','physically ill/sick The thought made her feel physically ill.','physically exhausted We were mentally and physically exhausted.','physically attractive She found him physically attractive.','physically capable of doing something Any one of them would have been physically capable of committing the crime.','physically abuse somebody Her father had physically abused her.','physically attack somebody It was the first time he had ever physically attacked anybody.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She is young and physically fit.","translation":"او جوان است و از نظر بدنی آماده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000357873.mp3"},{"sentence":"Do you find him physically attractive?","translation":"آیا او را از نظر فیزیکی جذاب می دانید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566309.mp3"},{"sentence":"I felt physically sick at the thought.","translation":"با این فکر احساس بیماری جسمی کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000357874.mp3"},{"sentence":"children who have been physically abused","translation":"کودکانی که مورد آزار جسمی قرار گرفته اند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566310.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('9b444b99-5a4a-5414-9c37-19a1a749bbf1','7593498d-7d3c-5eb8-ae01-ef762c65336d',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'physically possible/impossible','به‌طور بدنی، جسمی؛ از نظر فیزیکی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['physically fit It is important to keep yourself physically fit.','physically active He remained physically active far into old age.','physically disabled The attack left her physically disabled.','physically ill/sick The thought made her feel physically ill.','physically exhausted We were mentally and physically exhausted.','physically attractive She found him physically attractive.','physically capable of doing something Any one of them would have been physically capable of committing the crime.','physically abuse somebody Her father had physically abused her.','physically attack somebody It was the first time he had ever physically attacked anybody.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('86fb4d7a-095a-5923-a7de-638057b36e87','0175e677-1a74-5c3b-9658-daed6966703f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','someone who works in politics , especially an elected member of the government',null,null,'سیاست‌مدار، سیاست‌پیشه؛ نماینده مجلس','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a Labour/Republican etc politician Her mother was a Labour politician.','an opposition politician (= belonging to the party that is not in power – used in some political systems ) Opposition politicians argued that there was not enough reason to go to war.','a left-wing/right-wing politician He had been under attack from right-wing politicians for some time.','a leading/prominent politician The scandal ruined the careers of several leading politicians.','a senior politician Talks between senior politicians in Zagreb and Belgrade took place.','a local politician The plan is strongly supported by local politicians.','an elected politician Are the country’s elected politicians trustworthy?','popular He is the most popular politician in the country.','corrupt (= one who is not honest ) They make quiet deals with corrupt politicians.','astute/shrewd (= one who is good at getting what he wants done ) He proved to be an astute politician.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"politicians who are trying to get the minority vote","translation":"سیاستمدارانی که در تلاش برای به دست آوردن رأی اقلیت هستند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001574106.mp3"},{"sentence":"a British Labour politician","translation":"یک سیاستمدار کارگر بریتانیایی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001574109.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('e63f5776-a436-55a5-81c3-0c71e2fcc519','0175e677-1a74-5c3b-9658-daed6966703f',2,null,null,'spoken & written','someone who is skilled at dealing with people or using the situation within an organization to gain an advantage',null,null,'کسی که در برخورد با افراد یا استفاده از موقعیت درون سازمانی برای کسب مزیت مهارت دارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a Labour/Republican etc politician Her mother was a Labour politician.','an opposition politician (= belonging to the party that is not in power – used in some political systems ) Opposition politicians argued that there was not enough reason to go to war.','a left-wing/right-wing politician He had been under attack from right-wing politicians for some time.','a leading/prominent politician The scandal ruined the careers of several leading politicians.','a senior politician Talks between senior politicians in Zagreb and Belgrade took place.','a local politician The plan is strongly supported by local politicians.','an elected politician Are the country’s elected politicians trustworthy?','popular He is the most popular politician in the country.','corrupt (= one who is not honest ) They make quiet deals with corrupt politicians.','astute/shrewd (= one who is good at getting what he wants done ) He proved to be an astute politician.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the office politician","translation":"سیاستمدار دفتر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000345961.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('19e89b3c-193c-5dd8-86a6-d228c4a95d87','303616e6-a888-527c-b366-b7c96c374b91',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the number of people living in a particular area, country etc','[ countable ]',null,'جمعیت، نُهیت (کشور)؛ جمعیت (بومی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the total/whole/entire population The entire population will be celebrating.','the world''s population Sixty percent of the world''s population live in areas that are at risk from sea-level rises.','the general population Ethnic minorities suffer more than the general population.','the local population The local population gave them a warm welcome.','the black/white population (= black or white people who live in a place ) Unemployment is greater among the black population.','the Jewish/Muslim/Asian etc population (= the people of a particular nationality or religion who live in a place ) the city''s 4,000-strong Asian population','the indigenous population formal (= the people who have always lived in a place ) His new book assesses the impact of Spanish culture on the indigenous population of Mexico.','the urban population (= the people who live in towns or cities ) The region''s urban population will more than double in the next two decades.','the rural population (= the people who live in the countryside ) Agricultural reforms must address the needs of the rural population.','the adult population A third of the adult population pay no tax at all.','the elderly population Should the entire elderly population be regularly screened for this disease?','an ageing population (= gradually becoming older on average ) The rapidly ageing population will put a strain on the country''s health care system.','a large population California is a big state with a large population.','a prison population (= the number of people in prisons in a country or area ) A quarter of the prison population is under 21.','a student population The university has a student population of almost 5,000.','a population grows/increases/rises Between these years the population grew by 40%.','a population falls/declines/decreases The population in many rural areas has continued to fall.','a population reaches Nigeria ''s population will reach 532 million in the middle of this century.','population growth Rapid population growth intensifies competition for land.','population increase The population increase in the region is a cause for concern.','a population explosion/boom (= when the population increases quickly and by a large amount ) What will be the long-term effects of this population explosion?','population density (= the degree to which an area is filled with people ) Australia has a low population density.','population control (= controlling how many children people have ) It is argued that population control is essential to limit the depletion of natural resources.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"India has a population of more than one billion.","translation":"هند بیش از یک میلیارد جمعیت دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa020178.mp3"},{"sentence":"Nearly 70 percent of the population still live in the countryside.","translation":"نزدیک به 70 درصد از جمعیت هنوز در روستا زندگی می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001232.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('2284a5eb-edc5-502b-8dc2-ad6457a1770f','303616e6-a888-527c-b366-b7c96c374b91',2,null,null,'spoken & written','all of the people who live in a particular area','[ countable usually singular ]',null,'همه افرادی که در یک منطقه خاص زندگی می کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the total/whole/entire population The entire population will be celebrating.','the world''s population Sixty percent of the world''s population live in areas that are at risk from sea-level rises.','the general population Ethnic minorities suffer more than the general population.','the local population The local population gave them a warm welcome.','the black/white population (= black or white people who live in a place ) Unemployment is greater among the black population.','the Jewish/Muslim/Asian etc population (= the people of a particular nationality or religion who live in a place ) the city''s 4,000-strong Asian population','the indigenous population formal (= the people who have always lived in a place ) His new book assesses the impact of Spanish culture on the indigenous population of Mexico.','the urban population (= the people who live in towns or cities ) The region''s urban population will more than double in the next two decades.','the rural population (= the people who live in the countryside ) Agricultural reforms must address the needs of the rural population.','the adult population A third of the adult population pay no tax at all.','the elderly population Should the entire elderly population be regularly screened for this disease?','an ageing population (= gradually becoming older on average ) The rapidly ageing population will put a strain on the country''s health care system.','a large population California is a big state with a large population.','a prison population (= the number of people in prisons in a country or area ) A quarter of the prison population is under 21.','a student population The university has a student population of almost 5,000.','a population grows/increases/rises Between these years the population grew by 40%.','a population falls/declines/decreases The population in many rural areas has continued to fall.','a population reaches Nigeria ''s population will reach 532 million in the middle of this century.','population growth Rapid population growth intensifies competition for land.','population increase The population increase in the region is a cause for concern.','a population explosion/boom (= when the population increases quickly and by a large amount ) What will be the long-term effects of this population explosion?','population density (= the degree to which an area is filled with people ) Australia has a low population density.','population control (= controlling how many children people have ) It is argued that population control is essential to limit the depletion of natural resources.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Most of the world’s population doesn’t get enough to eat.","translation":"اکثر جمعیت جهان به اندازه کافی غذا نمی خورند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000309727.mp3"},{"sentence":"South Florida has a large Jewish population.","translation":"فلوریدا جنوبی جمعیت زیادی از یهودیان دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001636532.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('7a650d20-72dc-54a4-b09f-cc63a74d8c29','303616e6-a888-527c-b366-b7c96c374b91',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'centre of population/population centre','جمعیت، نُهیت (کشور)؛ جمعیت (بومی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('d58a8cd5-f1ac-57d8-92c8-48bb0ba94992','f0637b61-3480-584a-ba01-4e4c4960ea63',1,'having something','داشتن چیزی','formal','if something is in your possession, you own it, or you have obtained it from somewhere','[ uncountable ]',null,'مالکیت، دارایی؛ تسلط (بر خود)؛ ولایت (جنون)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be in somebody''s possession The painting has been in the family''s possession since then.','come into somebody''s possession You have a duty not to disclose confidential information that comes into your possession.','be in possession of something (= have it ) Before applying for a job, make sure you are in possession of the required qualifications.','have something in your possession (= have it ) My father had in his possession a letter written by Winston Churchill.','come into possession of something (= start having it ) How did you come into possession of this document?','take possession of something (= start having or using it ) At 21, he was entitled to take possession of the property.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The house has been in the family’s possession since the 1500s.","translation":"این خانه از سال 1500 در اختیار خانواده بوده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000312517.mp3"},{"sentence":"That information is not in our possession.","translation":"این اطلاعات در اختیار ما نیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000312522.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was found in possession of stolen goods.","translation":"او با داشتن اجناس مسروقه کشف شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000312521.mp3"},{"sentence":"How did the painting come into your possession (= how did you get it ) ?","translation":"چگونه نقاشی در اختیار شما قرار گرفت (= چگونه آن را به دست آوردید)؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000312526.mp3"},{"sentence":"The finance company now has possession of the house.","translation":"شرکت مالی اکنون خانه را در اختیار دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000312530.mp3"},{"sentence":"We didn’t take possession of (= get and start using ) the car until a few days after the auction.","translation":"ما ماشین را تا چند روز پس از حراج تصاحب نکردیم (= دریافت و شروع به استفاده از آن).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001763454.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('e46eaddb-6832-5447-8a02-b4cb4b481048','f0637b61-3480-584a-ba01-4e4c4960ea63',2,'something you own','چیزی که شما مالک آن هستید','spoken & written','something that you own or have with you at a particular time','[ countable usually plural ]',null,'چیزی که مالک آن هستید یا در یک زمان خاص همراه خود دارید',array['belongings']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He had sold all his possessions and left the country.","translation":"تمام دارایی خود را فروخته بود و کشور را ترک کرده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000312506.mp3"},{"sentence":"I packed my remaining possessions into the trunk.","translation":"من باقی مانده ام را در صندوق عقب جمع کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000312507.mp3"},{"sentence":"This old violin had been her father’s most treasured possession.","translation":"این ویولن قدیمی با ارزش ترین دارایی پدرش بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001576663.mp3"},{"sentence":"Prisoners were allowed no personal possessions .","translation":"زندانیان اجازه نداشتند دارایی شخصی داشته باشند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001576667.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('7e00468b-56f4-5cd0-a032-dfa5481acc94','f0637b61-3480-584a-ba01-4e4c4960ea63',3,'crime','جنایت','law','the crime of having illegal drugs or weapons with you or in your home','[ uncountable ]',null,'جرم داشتن مواد مخدر یا اسلحه غیرقانونی با خود یا در خانه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He was arrested and charged with possession of cocaine.","translation":"او دستگیر و متهم به نگهداری کوکائین شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001576673.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('f0c96309-9c6b-5722-b669-84b6286611d9','f0637b61-3480-584a-ba01-4e4c4960ea63',4,'sport','ورزش','spoken & written','when a person or team has control of the ball in some sports','[ uncountable ]',null,'زمانی که یک فرد یا تیم کنترل توپ را در برخی از ورزش ها در اختیار دارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Pittsburgh got possession and scored.","translation":"پیتسبورگ صاحب توپ شد و گل زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000312557.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('dadd5127-763a-5e82-ae3f-0cee63497dba','f0637b61-3480-584a-ba01-4e4c4960ea63',5,'country','کشور','spoken & written','a country controlled or governed by another country','[ countable usually plural ]',null,'کشوری که توسط کشور دیگری کنترل یا اداره می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"France’s former colonial possessions","translation":"دارایی های استعماری سابق فرانسه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000312548.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('9ff24ff0-02b6-5c46-8451-539bc8472eb9','f0637b61-3480-584a-ba01-4e4c4960ea63',6,'evil spirits','ارواح شیطانی','spoken & written','a situation in which someone’s mind is being controlled by something evil','[ uncountable ]',null,'موقعیتی که در آن ذهن کسی توسط چیزی بد کنترل می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Was it a case of demonic possession?","translation":"آیا این یک مورد تسخیر شیطانی بود؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000312573.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('6e2523c3-d2fc-521e-ba8d-a9843644935c','f0637b61-3480-584a-ba01-4e4c4960ea63',7,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'in (full) possession of your faculties/senses','مالکیت، دارایی؛ تسلط (بر خود)؛ ولایت (جنون)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
