('a0744c4a-00c2-5cfe-aac6-9debb69e9d42','68a6602e-bec4-5217-a365-70eeb7ae35e7',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the study of the mind and how it influences people’s behaviour','[ uncountable ]',null,'روان‌شناسی، علم روان؛ رفتار (روانی)؛ ذهن (روان)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"experts in the field of developmental psychology","translation":"متخصصان روانشناسی رشد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001766463.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ae335643-7daa-58a9-afcc-b5ae481dcd99','68a6602e-bec4-5217-a365-70eeb7ae35e7',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the mental processes involved in believing in something or doing a certain activity','[ uncountable ]',null,'فرآیندهای ذهنی مربوط به اعتقاد به چیزی یا انجام یک فعالیت خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"research into the psychology of racism","translation":"تحقیق در مورد روانشناسی نژادپرستی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001561698.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c7c13e03-16c3-56ba-8c48-238335c984b4','68a6602e-bec4-5217-a365-70eeb7ae35e7',3,null,null,'spoken & written','what someone thinks or believes, and how this affects what they do','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'اینکه یک نفر چه فکر می‌کند یا به آن اعتقاد دارد، و این که چگونه بر کاری که انجام می‌دهد تأثیر می‌گذارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the psychology of three-year-olds","translation":"روانشناسی کودکان سه ساله","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000269594.mp3"},{"sentence":"mob psychology","translation":"روانشناسی اوباش","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001561699.mp3"},{"sentence":"You have to use psychology to get people to stop smoking.","translation":"شما باید از روانشناسی استفاده کنید تا مردم سیگار را ترک کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001561700.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('4a9070b5-e6fe-5306-af0e-2a971253a20d','728a65bc-417a-5a73-b870-4e1caf09ec6e',1,null,null,'spoken & written','something that is done in order to punish someone, or the act of punishing them','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'مجازات، کیفر؛ مجازات (بدنی)؛ مجازات (روانی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['harsh/severe The court decided the original punishment was too severe.','light The punishment seemed very light.','just/fitting (= appropriate and right ) Death would be a just punishment.','physical punishment Children respond more to affection than to physical punishment.','corporal punishment (= when someone punishes a child by hitting them ) Corporal punishment is banned in state schools.','capital punishment (= death as a punishment for a crime ) The are trying to abolish capital punishment except in cases of terrorism.','the maximum punishment The charge against him carries a maximum punishment of a year in jail.','give somebody a punishment He deserved the punishment he was given. The teacher may impose reasonable punishments.','hand out punishments (= give people punishments ) The courts are handing out harsher punishments to reckless drivers.','impose/mete out a punishment formal (= give someone a punishment ) Life imprisonment should be the maximum punishment meted out by the state.','receive a punishment He received the maximum punishment.','escape/avoid punishment The thieves managed to escape punishment.','carry a punishment (= used when saying what the punishment for something is ) The offence carries a punishment of up to 10 years in prison.','inflict a punishment (on somebody) (= punish someone, especially physically ) The abbot could inflict corporal punishment for gross disobedience.','the punishment should fit the crime (= it should be appropriate ) The public believe that the punishment should fit the crime.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The punishment for treason is death.","translation":"مجازات خیانت اعدام است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001269.mp3"},{"sentence":"I was sent to bed as a punishment.","translation":"من را به عنوان مجازات به رختخواب فرستادند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001540006.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('bebf33d9-385d-5804-9f87-729130b36af6','728a65bc-417a-5a73-b870-4e1caf09ec6e',2,null,null,'informal','rough physical treatment','[ uncountable ]',null,'درمان فیزیکی خشن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['harsh/severe The court decided the original punishment was too severe.','light The punishment seemed very light.','just/fitting (= appropriate and right ) Death would be a just punishment.','physical punishment Children respond more to affection than to physical punishment.','corporal punishment (= when someone punishes a child by hitting them ) Corporal punishment is banned in state schools.','capital punishment (= death as a punishment for a crime ) The are trying to abolish capital punishment except in cases of terrorism.','the maximum punishment The charge against him carries a maximum punishment of a year in jail.','give somebody a punishment He deserved the punishment he was given. The teacher may impose reasonable punishments.','hand out punishments (= give people punishments ) The courts are handing out harsher punishments to reckless drivers.','impose/mete out a punishment formal (= give someone a punishment ) Life imprisonment should be the maximum punishment meted out by the state.','receive a punishment He received the maximum punishment.','escape/avoid punishment The thieves managed to escape punishment.','carry a punishment (= used when saying what the punishment for something is ) The offence carries a punishment of up to 10 years in prison.','inflict a punishment (on somebody) (= punish someone, especially physically ) The abbot could inflict corporal punishment for gross disobedience.','the punishment should fit the crime (= it should be appropriate ) The public believe that the punishment should fit the crime.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"tough plants that can take any amount of punishment","translation":"گیاهان سختی که می توانند هر نوع مجازاتی را تحمل کنند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000277921.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c38590de-627f-50e3-b8e1-95e78cc03e0a','bcb73ba0-40fd-5875-8e18-8e9649c3bd25',1,null,null,'spoken & written','fair and sensible',null,null,'معقول، منطقی؛ منصفانه (بها)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['perfectly/entirely reasonable ( also eminently reasonable formal ) (= completely reasonable ) The proposal sounds perfectly reasonable.','reasonable enough (= fairly reasonable ) It was a reasonable enough question.','a reasonable explanation/excuse He tried to think of a reasonable excuse.','a reasonable request He had refused to obey a reasonable request from a senior member of staff.','a reasonable question Here is one possible answer to that very reasonable question.','a reasonable assumption It is a reasonable assumption that he pressed the wrong button.','reasonable grounds (= good reasons ) She must show that she had some reasonable grounds for her action.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a reasonable request","translation":"یک درخواست منطقی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000485641.mp3"},{"sentence":"Be reasonable – you can’t expect her to do all the work on her own!","translation":"منطقی باشید - نمی توانید از او انتظار داشته باشید که همه کارها را خودش انجام دهد!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000485640.mp3"},{"sentence":"I thought it was a perfectly reasonable (= completely reasonable ) question.","translation":"من فکر کردم که این یک سؤال کاملاً منطقی (= کاملاً منطقی) است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985988.mp3"},{"sentence":"It seems reasonable to assume they’ve been tested.","translation":"منطقی به نظر می رسد که فرض کنیم آنها آزمایش شده اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604696.mp3"},{"sentence":"He had reasonable grounds (= good reasons but no proof ) for believing the law had been broken.","translation":"او دلایل معقولی (= دلایل خوب اما بدون دلیل) داشت که معتقد بود قانون نقض شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604703.mp3"},{"sentence":"It sounded like a reasonable enough excuse to me.","translation":"به نظرم بهانه ای معقول بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985995.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('e027db78-b5bc-571e-ae46-fda32a6ad83a','bcb73ba0-40fd-5875-8e18-8e9649c3bd25',2,null,null,'spoken & written','fairly good, but not especially good',null,null,'نسبتا خوب است، اما نه به خصوص خوب',array['average']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['perfectly/entirely reasonable ( also eminently reasonable formal ) (= completely reasonable ) The proposal sounds perfectly reasonable.','reasonable enough (= fairly reasonable ) It was a reasonable enough question.','a reasonable explanation/excuse He tried to think of a reasonable excuse.','a reasonable request He had refused to obey a reasonable request from a senior member of staff.','a reasonable question Here is one possible answer to that very reasonable question.','a reasonable assumption It is a reasonable assumption that he pressed the wrong button.','reasonable grounds (= good reasons ) She must show that she had some reasonable grounds for her action.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She has a reasonable chance of doing well in the exam.","translation":"او شانس معقولی برای موفقیت در امتحان دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000485652.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
